//@version=6
// ============================================================================
// ShapeMap v0.9.2  |  TOP-03 of the VT Markets screen  |  XAUUSD-ECNc M15
// Settings: Turn_AfterHold, Points_default, lossrev any_notiny, filter off
// Screen (VT XAUUSD-ECNc real bid/ask ticks, July 2026, 0.10 cent lot, 0.60 USD round trip per lot):
//   trades 64  net 26.09 USD  PF 2.00  win 73%  maxDD 7.07 USD  positive weeks 80%  halves 6.86/19.23
// Costs in strategy(): commission 0.30 USD per contract per side (= VT 0.60 round trip per cent lot of 1 oz),
//   slippage 10 ticks per side (~half of the 13-tick VT spread + ~3 ticks execution), quantity 0.1 contracts = 0.10 cent lot.
// Chart: XAUUSD, timeframe M15. TradingView's feed is not VT's tick feed; expect different fills.
// This is a 4-week screen, not a calibration: 20-110 trades, one month, no out-of-sample test. Treat as a candidate only.
// Hard-coded input defaults (everything else is the author's default):
//   sigMode = "Turn ▲/▼"
//   turnEntry = "After hold (when ▲/▼ confirms)"
//   exitUnit = "Points"
//   slPts = 7000.0
//   tpPts = 50000.0
//   trailOn = true
//   trActPts = 1000.0
//   trDisPts = 100.0
//   lossRevOn = true
//   lossRevWhat = "Any losing exit"
//   lossRevTiny = false
//   lossRevMax = 1
//   lossRevTinyPts = 1500.0
//   qtyMode = "Fixed"
//   qtyFixed = 0.1
//   fgfOn = false
//   fgfSpreadPts = 13.0
// XPW Shape Map v0.9.2 strategy source as supplied, unchanged except the input defaults and strategy() costs listed above.
// ============================================================================
// XPW Shape Map v0.9.2 STRATEGY
// Built from the XPW Shape Map v0.6 indicator. Same detection, same labels.
// ONE entry signal at a time — pick it in "S1. Entry". Signals are never mixed:
//   BOT/TOP square  -> BOT square = LONG,  TOP square = SHORT
//   Turn ▲/▼        -> Turn ▲     = LONG,  Turn ▼     = SHORT
//   BOT/TOP tick    -> BOT tick   = LONG,  TOP tick   = SHORT
//   CONT ▲/▼        -> CONT ▲     = LONG,  CONT ▼     = SHORT   (new in v0.9)
// Turn entries default to PREDICT: at each candle close the exact price where
// fast and slow would cross on the next candle is calculated and a stop order
// sits there, so the entry fills the moment price reaches the cross — live and
// in the backtest. Blue dots on the price chart show that price.
// "Enter on tick" ON (default): live, the strategy runs every tick and enters the
// moment the signal appears inside the forming candle — no wait for the close.
// On history there are no ticks, so backtests still enter on the next bar's open.
// Margin is set to 1% (100:1, like a CFD account). With TradingView's default
// 100% margin, 10 oz of gold costs more than a $10k account and every order is
// silently rejected. Change it in Properties -> Margin if your broker differs.
// "Points" = minimum ticks (XAUUSD: 1 pt = 0.01, so 5000 pts = $50).
//
// v0.7 — entry calibration, no missed entries:
//   * Predict buffer: move the stop N ticks past (+) or ahead of (-) the cross
//     price. A small + buffer filters wicks that touch the cross and fail
//     ("cross failed" exits); a - buffer gets in earlier.
//   * Catch missed crosses: if the cross happens at a candle close but the
//     stop did not fill (cross more than one candle away when the stop was
//     priced, gap, rounding), enter at that close instead of skipping it.
//   * Predict arms on "Every cross": trade every fast/slow cross, not only the
//     ones that follow a BOT/TOP square.
//   * Margin cap: quantity is cut to what the account's margin allows, so
//     orders are not silently rejected after a drawdown (10 BTC at 1% margin
//     needs ~$8.7k — on a $10k account one losing streak blocked every entry).
//
// v0.8 — drawdown calibration (OKX BTCUSDT 15m / 30m / 1H, Aug–Oct 2026):
//   * Sizing defaults to Risk % = 1% of equity per trade. The old fixed 10 BTC
//     with a $500 stop risked ~50% of a $10k account on one trade
//     (max DD 29–74%). At 1% risk max DD was 1.7–4.6% on every timeframe.
//   * Stop loss 7000 pts ($700 at 0.1 tick), trail starts at 1000 pts ($100)
//     and trails 100 pts ($10), predict buffer 100 pts ($10).
//   * "Exit if the cross fails" defaults OFF: those early exits lost money on
//     every timeframe once fees were counted.
//   * Commission 0.05% per side (OKX taker) so the backtest shows real costs.
//     With 0 commission the same settings look ~3x better than they are.
//
// v0.9 — CONT: continuation WITHOUT a cross (from Shape Map indicator v0.7):
//   * New entry signal "CONT ▲/▼". CONT ▲ (long) is the sequence calibrated on
//     BITGET BTCUSDT 30m (9 Oct and 11 Oct 2026, 07:30 -> 10:00):
//       1. big GREEN candle (body >= 1.0 ATR)
//       2. a LITTLE RED area right after it (<= 12 bars)
//       3. that red area PINCHES to a tiny gap (<= 1.0 RSI pts) and flips GREEN
//       4. the first GREEN candle while the fill is STILL green (no cross back)
//     CONT ▼ (short) is the exact mirror. Both draw their own aqua / fuchsia
//     labels and have their own counters; every other label is unchanged.
//   * CONT entry timing: "At signal close" (market, or on tick) or "Stop past
//     signal candle" (buy stop above the CONT candle's high / sell stop below
//     its low, cancelled if not filled within N bars).
//   * Exits, sizing, margin cap and opposite-signal handling are shared with
//     the other signals, so CONT trades use the same SL / TP / trail.
//
// v0.9.1 — LOSS REVERSAL: open the opposite trade when a trade exits in the red:
//   * New group "S4. Loss reversal". When a trade closes with a negative P&L
//     (stop loss, trailing stop under the entry, time stop, failed cross...),
//     the strategy immediately opens a trade in the OTHER direction, with the
//     normal quantity and the same SL / TP / trail. A long that lost becomes a
//     short, a short that lost becomes a long. A trade that closed with a real
//     profit never triggers it (a tiny profit can, see below).
//   * "Which exits count": any losing exit, or only the stop loss / trailing
//     stop. "Max reversals in a row" (default 1) stops the ping-pong: after N
//     reversal trades in a row that also lost, the strategy waits for the next
//     real signal. A reversal trade that WINS resets the count.
//   * Live with "Enter on tick" the reversal fires on the first tick after the
//     losing exit is seen; on history it fills at the close of the exit candle.
//     "Trade direction" is respected: with "Long only" a losing long is not
//     reversed into a short.
//   * The reversal trade uses the normal "Long" / "Short" order ids, so the
//     usual exits, the opposite-signal handling and the counters treat it like
//     any other trade. Its entry comment is "L loss-rev" / "S loss-rev".
//   * "Also reverse on a tiny profit": a trade that closes in the green but
//     moved no more than N points from entry to exit (a trailing stop that
//     fired right after it armed, a time stop at break-even...) counts as a
//     loss and is reversed too. The move is measured in price points, so it
//     does not depend on the quantity or the commission.
//
// v0.9.2 — SIGNAL TIMEFRAME: run the entry logic on a timeframe you pick:
//   * New input "Signal timeframe" in "S1. Entry" (blank = the chart's own
//     timeframe, which is exactly v0.9.1). The WHOLE detection — TDI lines,
//     areas, BOT/TOP squares, Turn ▲/▼, ticks, CONT and the Predict cross
//     price — is calculated on THAT timeframe with request.security(), while
//     the orders, the exits (SL / TP / trail / time stop), the sizing and the
//     loss reversal keep running on the chart's candles. Example: signal
//     timeframe "10" on a 15 min chart -> the entries are the 10 min signals,
//     the trade is managed candle by candle on the 15 min chart. SL / TP /
//     trail in points are price distances, so they mean the same on any
//     timeframe.
//   * Every signal is an EVENT stamped with the time of the signal-timeframe
//     candle it fired on, so a 1H signal on a 15 min chart fires ONCE, not on
//     each of the four 15 min candles the 1H candle covers.
//   * Higher signal timeframe (1H signals on a 15 min chart): on history the
//     signal arrives on the chart candle where the 1H candle closes. Live,
//     with "Enter on tick", it can arrive inside the forming 1H candle (and,
//     like any on-tick signal, it can still disappear before that candle
//     closes; the trade stays open anyway).
//   * Lower signal timeframe (5 min signals on a 15 min chart): the chart
//     candle receives the signals of its intrabars and acts on them at its
//     close on history (on tick live). Best with a signal timeframe that
//     divides the chart timeframe (5 on 15, 15 on 60...). "10" on a 15 min
//     chart works, but the 10 min candles straddle the 15 min ones, so a
//     signal can show up one chart candle late. TradingView keeps a limited
//     intrabar history, so such backtests reach less far back.
//   * Labels are drawn on the chart candle where the signal arrives (the
//     square box / turn mark are shifted back by the signal's "bars" scaled to
//     chart candles). Settings in "bars" that belong to the SIGNAL (context,
//     width, min bars between, max bars to wait, cross must hold, CONT bars)
//     count signal-timeframe candles. Settings in bars that belong to the
//     TRADE (time stop, CONT stop valid for N bars) count chart candles; the
//     "cross failed" check converts the hold bars to chart candles.
//   * The panel plots the signal timeframe's fast / slow lines and fill, so
//     the labels sit on the lines that produced them. The table shows the
//     signal timeframe next to the chart timeframe.

strategy("ShapeMap v0.9.2 S | VT XAUUSD M15 #03", shorttitle = "SM92 03 M15", overlay = false, max_boxes_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500, max_lines_count = 500, max_bars_back = 500, pyramiding = 0, calc_on_every_tick = true, process_orders_on_close = true, initial_capital = 10000, default_qty_type = strategy.fixed, default_qty_value = 0.1, margin_long = 1, margin_short = 1, commission_type = strategy.commission.cash_per_contract, commission_value = 0.30, slippage = 10)

// ───────────────────────── S1. ENTRY ─────────────────────────
grpE = "S1. Entry"
sigMode  = input.string("Turn ▲/▼", "Entry signal (one only)", options = ["BOT/TOP square", "Turn ▲/▼", "BOT/TOP tick", "CONT ▲/▼"], group = grpE, tooltip = "Only this pair of labels opens trades. BOT / ▲ side = long, TOP / ▼ side = short. The other labels still draw but never trade. CONT ▲/▼ = continuation without a cross (big candle -> little odd area -> pinch -> candle in trend direction).")
sigTF    = input.timeframe("", "Signal timeframe (blank = chart)", group = grpE, tooltip = "Timeframe the entry logic runs on. Blank = the chart's timeframe (v0.9.1 behaviour). Example: 10 on a 15 min chart -> the signals (TDI, squares, turns, ticks, CONT, predict price) come from the 10 min candles, while the trade (SL / TP / trail / time stop, sizing, loss reversal) is managed on the 15 min chart candles. A higher timeframe signal arrives on the chart candle where that higher candle closes (on history) or inside it (live, 'Enter on tick'). A lower timeframe signal is acted on at the chart candle's close (history) or on tick (live). Prefer a timeframe that divides the chart timeframe (5 on 15, 15 on 60).")
tradeDir = input.string("Both", "Trade direction", options = ["Both", "Long only", "Short only"], group = grpE)
enterTick = input.bool(true, "Enter on tick (don't wait for candle close)", group = grpE, tooltip = "ON: in realtime the script runs on every tick and enters the moment the signal appears inside the forming candle. The signal can still disappear before the candle closes; the trade stays open anyway. OFF: wait for the candle to close and fill on the next candle's open. On history there are no ticks, so the backtest always uses closed candles.")
turnEntry = input.string("After hold (when ▲/▼ confirms)", "Turn entry timing", options = ["Predict (stop at cross price)", "At the cross", "After hold (when ▲/▼ confirms)"], group = grpE, tooltip = "Predict: at each candle close the strategy calculates the exact price where fast would cross slow on the next candle and places a stop order there. It fills the instant price gets there — live and in the backtest. At the cross: enter when the cross is seen (candle close, or on tick if 'Enter on tick' is on). After hold: wait until the cross has held for 'Bars the cross must hold'.")
failExit  = input.bool(false, "Turn: exit if the cross fails to hold", group = grpE, tooltip = "Predict / At the cross. If at a candle close the lines are back on the wrong side within 'Bars the cross must hold' candles of entry, close the trade.")
oppMode  = input.string("Reverse", "Opposite signal while in a trade", options = ["Reverse", "Close only", "Ignore"], group = grpE, tooltip = "Reverse: close and open the other side. Close only: close and wait. Ignore: let the exits handle it.")

// ─────────────────── S1b. PREDICT CALIBRATION ───────────────────
grpC = "S1b. Predict calibration"
armMode  = input.string("Squares (BOT/TOP)", "Predict arms on", options = ["Squares (BOT/TOP)", "Every cross"], group = grpC, tooltip = "Squares: a stop is only placed after a BOT square (long) or TOP square (short), for 'Max bars to wait after a square'. Every cross: a stop always sits at the next cross price, so no cross is missed.")
predBuf  = input.float(100, "Predict buffer, pts (+ = past the cross, - = earlier)", group = grpC, tooltip = "Moves the stop away from the exact cross price. +N: price must go N ticks beyond the cross — fewer fills on wicks that touch the cross and fail. -N: fill N ticks before the cross — earlier entry, more false starts.")
catchUp  = input.bool(true, "Catch missed crosses at candle close", group = grpC, tooltip = "If the lines cross at a candle close but the stop did not fill (the cross was more than one candle away when the stop was priced, a gap, rounding), enter at that close instead of missing the trade.")
maxChase = input.float(0, "Catch-up: max chase from cross price, pts (0 = no limit)", minval = 0, group = grpC, tooltip = "Skip the catch-up entry if the close is already further than this beyond the predicted cross price.")

// ─────────────────── S1c. CONT ENTRY (v0.9) ───────────────────
grpCE = "S1c. CONT entry"
contEntry   = input.string("At signal close", "CONT entry timing", options = ["At signal close", "Stop past signal candle"], group = grpCE, tooltip = "At signal close: market order on the CONT candle (on tick if 'Enter on tick' is on). Stop past signal candle: buy stop above the CONT candle's high (sell stop below its low) plus the buffer, so the trade only starts if price keeps going. The CONT candle is the SIGNAL timeframe's candle.")
contStopBuf = input.float(50, "CONT stop buffer, pts past the candle", minval = 0, group = grpCE)
contStopBars = input.int(3, "CONT stop valid for N bars, then cancel", minval = 1, group = grpCE, tooltip = "Chart candles.")

// Backtest: process_orders_on_close fills at the signal candle's close instead of
// the next candle's open, so history entries sit on the label's candle.
// Signals may fire on any tick (enterTick ON) or only on a closed candle.
sigBarOK = enterTick or barstate.isconfirmed

// ───────────────────────── S2. EXITS ─────────────────────────
grpX = "S2. Exits"
exitUnit = input.string("Points", "SL / TP / trail unit", options = ["Points", "ATR"], group = grpX)
slPts    = input.float(7000.0,  "Stop loss, pts (Points mode)",   minval = 0, group = grpX, tooltip = "1 pt = 1 minimum tick. 0 = no stop loss.")
tpPts    = input.float(50000.0, "Take profit, pts (Points mode)", minval = 0, group = grpX, tooltip = "1 pt = 1 minimum tick. 0 = no take profit.")
exAtrLen = input.int(14,      "ATR length (ATR mode)", minval = 1, group = grpX)
slAtrM   = input.float(2.0,   "Stop loss, ATR mult (ATR mode)", minval = 0, step = 0.1, group = grpX)
tpR      = input.float(2.0,   "Take profit, R multiple of SL (ATR mode)", minval = 0, step = 0.1, group = grpX)
trailOn  = input.bool(true,   "Trailing stop", group = grpX)
trActPts = input.float(1000.0,  "Trail activation, pts of profit (Points mode)", minval = 0, group = grpX)
trDisPts = input.float(100.0,   "Trail distance, pts (Points mode)", minval = 0, group = grpX)
trActAtr = input.float(4.0,   "Trail activation, ATR mult (ATR mode)", minval = 0, step = 0.1, group = grpX)
trDisAtr = input.float(0.2,   "Trail distance, ATR mult (ATR mode)", minval = 0, step = 0.1, group = grpX)
timeStop = input.int(0,       "Time stop, bars (0 = off)", minval = 0, group = grpX, tooltip = "Chart candles.")

// ───────────────────────── S3. SIZING ─────────────────────────
grpZ = "S3. Sizing"
qtyMode  = input.string("Fixed", "Quantity", options = ["Fixed", "Risk %"], group = grpZ)
qtyFixed = input.float(0.1,  "Fixed quantity (contracts = oz, 100 = 1 lot)", minval = 0, group = grpZ)
riskPct  = input.float(1.0, "Risk % of equity per trade (Risk mode)", minval = 0, step = 0.1, group = grpZ, tooltip = "Quantity = equity x risk % / stop-loss distance. Needs a stop loss above 0.")
qtyMax   = input.float(50,  "Max quantity", minval = 0, group = grpZ)
qtyStep  = input.float(0.001, "Quantity step (rounds down)", minval = 0.00001, group = grpZ)
mgnCap   = input.bool(true, "Cap quantity to available margin", group = grpZ, tooltip = "Cuts the quantity to what the equity can carry at the margin below, so TradingView never silently rejects an entry.")
mgnPct   = input.float(1.0, "Margin % (match Properties -> Margin)", minval = 0.01, step = 0.1, group = grpZ)

// ───────────────────── S4. LOSS REVERSAL (v0.9.1) ─────────────────────
grpR = "S4. Loss reversal"
lossRevOn   = input.bool(true, "Open the opposite trade when a trade exits at a loss", group = grpR, tooltip = "A trade that closes with a negative P&L is immediately followed by a trade in the other direction (long lost -> short, short lost -> long), with the normal quantity and the same SL / TP / trail. A trade that closes with a real profit never triggers this (see 'tiny profit' below). 'Trade direction' is respected.")
lossRevWhat = input.string("Any losing exit", "Which exits count", options = ["Any losing exit", "Stop loss / trail only"], group = grpR, tooltip = "Any losing exit: stop loss, trailing stop under the entry, time stop, failed cross, opposite signal in 'Close only' mode... anything that closed in the red. Stop loss / trail only: just the SL and the trailing stop.")
lossRevMax  = input.int(1, "Max reversals in a row (0 = unlimited)", minval = 0, group = grpR, tooltip = "How many reversal trades may follow each other when they keep losing. 1 (default): one reversal per losing signal trade; if the reversal also loses, wait for the next real signal. A reversal trade that wins resets the count.")
lossRevTiny = input.bool(false, "Also reverse on a tiny profit", group = grpR, inline = "tp", tooltip = "A trade that closed in profit but moved no more than this many points from entry to exit (the trailing stop fired as soon as it armed, a time stop near break-even...) is treated like a loss and reversed. 1 pt = 1 minimum tick. A profit above this is a real winner and is never reversed.")
lossRevTinyPts = input.float(1500.0, "max pts", minval = 0, group = grpR, inline = "tp")

// ───────────────────────── TDI ─────────────────────────
grpT = "TDI"
rsiLen     = input.int(14,  "RSI length",     minval = 2, group = grpT)
fastLen    = input.int(2,   "Fast MA length", minval = 1, group = grpT)
slowLen    = input.int(7,   "Slow MA length", minval = 1, group = grpT)
invertFill = input.bool(true, "My panel paints fast>slow as RED", group = grpT)

// ───────────────────────── AREAS ─────────────────────────
grpA = "Areas"
areaLook = input.int(20,     "Area lookback", minval = 5, group = grpA)
loFrac   = input.float(0.20, "LOW area: below this fraction",  minval = 0.0, maxval = 1.0, step = 0.01, group = grpA)
hiFrac   = input.float(0.67, "HIGH area: above this fraction", minval = 0.0, maxval = 1.0, step = 0.01, group = grpA)

// ───────────────────── SHOW / HIDE ─────────────────────
// Turn individual drawings on/off. Detection, counts and the table keep running.
grpS = "Show / hide labels"
showBotBox   = input.bool(true, "BOT square box",        group = grpS, inline = "sb")
showBotLbl   = input.bool(true, "BOT square label",      group = grpS, inline = "sb")
showTopBox   = input.bool(true, "TOP square box",        group = grpS, inline = "st")
showTopLbl   = input.bool(true, "TOP square label",      group = grpS, inline = "st")
showTurnUp   = input.bool(true, "Turn ▲ (after BOT)",    group = grpS, inline = "tn")
showTurnDn   = input.bool(true, "Turn ▼ (after TOP)",    group = grpS, inline = "tn")
showBotTick  = input.bool(true, "BOT tick (price chart)", group = grpS, inline = "tk")
showTopTick  = input.bool(true, "TOP tick (price chart)", group = grpS, inline = "tk")
showContMark = input.bool(true, "CONT mark (panel)",      group = grpS, inline = "ct")
showContTick = input.bool(true, "CONT tick (price chart)", group = grpS, inline = "ct")

// ───────────────────── ALL OPPORTUNITIES ─────────────────────
// ON  = label every odd-colour wedge, anywhere, with no spacing.
// OFF = strict v0.5 rules (area + context + spacing from the groups below).
grpL = "Label ALL opportunities"
allOn  = input.bool(true, "Label ALL opportunities (ignore area + spacing)", group = grpL)
allCtx = input.int(1, "Context bars in ALL mode", minval = 1, group = grpL)

// ───────────────────── BOTTOM SQUARE ─────────────────────
grpB = "BOTTOM square (odd RED wedge, LOW area)"
botOn      = input.bool(true, "Enable",                   group = grpB)
botMinW    = input.int(1,  "Min width",     minval = 1,   group = grpB)
botMaxW    = input.int(3,  "Max width",     minval = 1,   group = grpB)
botCtxIn   = input.int(2,  "Context bars",  minval = 1,   group = grpB)
botNeedLow = input.bool(true, "Require LOW area",         group = grpB)
botSepIn   = input.int(5,  "Min bars between squares", minval = 0, group = grpB)

// ─────────────────────── TOP SQUARE ───────────────────────
grpP = "TOP square (odd LIME wedge, HIGH area)"
topOn       = input.bool(true, "Enable",                  group = grpP)
topMinW     = input.int(1,  "Min width",    minval = 1,   group = grpP)
topMaxW     = input.int(2,  "Max width",    minval = 1,   group = grpP)
topCtxIn    = input.int(3,  "Context bars", minval = 1,   group = grpP)
topNeedHigh = input.bool(true, "Require HIGH area",       group = grpP)
topSepIn    = input.int(5,  "Min bars between squares", minval = 0, group = grpP)

// Effective settings: ALL mode overrides context, area and spacing.
botCtx = allOn ? allCtx : botCtxIn
topCtx = allOn ? allCtx : topCtxIn
botSep = allOn ? 0 : botSepIn
topSep = allOn ? 0 : topSepIn

// ───────────────────────── TURN MARK ─────────────────────────
// The wedge warns. The turn confirms: the lines cross back and HOLD.
grpN = "Turn mark"
turnOn   = input.bool(true, "Enable",                       group = grpN)
turnMax  = input.int(12, "Max bars to wait after a square", minval = 1, group = grpN)
turnHold = input.int(2,  "Bars the cross must hold",        minval = 1, group = grpN)

// ──────────── TICKS (wick as a compressed cycle) ────────────
grpK = "Ticks"
tickOn       = input.bool(true, "Enable",                 group = grpK)
atrLen       = input.int(14, "ATR length", minval = 2,    group = grpK)
botWickRange = input.float(0.55, "BOTTOM: min lower wick / range", step = 0.05, group = grpK)
botWickAtr   = input.float(0.8,  "BOTTOM: min lower wick / ATR",   step = 0.10, group = grpK)
topWickRange = input.float(0.70, "TOP: min upper wick / range",    step = 0.05, group = grpK)
topWickAtr   = input.float(1.20, "TOP: min upper wick / ATR",      step = 0.10, group = grpK)

// ───────── CONT: continuation WITHOUT a cross (new in v0.9, from indicator v0.7) ─────────
// Long version (calibrated on BITGET BTCUSDT 30m, 9 Oct 07:30-10:00 and 11 Oct 07:30-10:00):
//   1. big GREEN candle (body >= N x ATR)                  -> 07:30 in both examples
//   2. a LITTLE RED area right after it (3 bars in both)   -> 08:00 .. 09:00
//   3. that red area PINCHES to an extremely small gap and the fill flips GREEN  -> 09:00/09:30
//   4. the first GREEN candle while the fill is STILL green (no cross back up)    -> 10:00
//   => "CONT ▲" on that green candle. The green candle may itself be big; that does
//      not restart the sequence.
// This is NOT a turn (no cross back happened) and NOT a BOT/TOP square (those stay
// exactly as before). It is its own mark, in its own colour, with its own counter.
grpCO = "CONT (continuation, no cross)"
contOn      = input.bool(true,  "Enable",                                              group = grpCO)
contBigAtr  = input.float(1.0,  "Big candle: min body / ATR",         step = 0.1, minval = 0.1, group = grpCO)
contLook    = input.int(30,     "Max bars from big candle to CONT",   minval = 2,  group = grpCO)
contNeedRed = input.bool(true,  "Require the little RED area after the big candle",     group = grpCO)
contRedMax  = input.int(12,     "Max bars of that little RED area",   minval = 1,  group = grpCO)
contPinch   = input.float(1.0,  "Pinch: max |fast-slow| where red flips to green (RSI pts)", step = 0.1, minval = 0.0, group = grpCO)
contAfter   = input.int(6,      "Max bars after the flip for the green candle", minval = 1, group = grpCO)
contSep     = input.int(5,      "Min bars between CONT marks",        minval = 0,  group = grpCO)
contMirror  = input.bool(true,  "Also detect the mirror (short) version: CONT ▼",      group = grpCO, tooltip = "Needed for shorts when the entry signal is CONT ▲/▼. Turn off to hide CONT ▼ and never short on it.")

// ───────────────────────── DISPLAY ─────────────────────────
grpD = "Display"
showTable = input.bool(true, "Show table", group = grpD)

// ===================== BEGIN FLASHGOLD DIRECTION FILTER ======================
// Set true when this block lives in a script that runs in its own pane
// (overlay=false) so the visuals are drawn on the price chart.
FGF_FORCE_OVERLAY = true

GRP_FGF = "Direction filter"
fgfOn        = input.bool(false, "Enable filter", group=GRP_FGF, tooltip="Off: buys and sells are always allowed. On: each FlashGold signal sets the level: BUY ZONE above it (+ the no-trade band), SELL ZONE below it (- the band), NO TRADE inside the band. Nothing is allowed before the first signal.")
fgfTf        = input.timeframe("60", "Filter timeframe", group=GRP_FGF, tooltip="The FlashGold signal runs on this timeframe's candles, and any chart (or strategy) using the filter gets the answer that timeframe's own chart shows at that moment: 1 hour on a 1m chart = the 1H view. Only closed candles are read, so nothing repaints. 'Chart' = this chart's own candles.")
fgfLvMode    = input.string("Entry price", "Level", options=["Entry price", "Signal close"], group=GRP_FGF, tooltip="Entry price: the FlashGold entry price of the signal (ask + entry distance for a BUY, bid - entry distance for a SELL). Signal close: the close of the signal candle.")
fgfLast      = input.string("Until next signal", "Permission lasts", options=["Until next signal", "Minutes", "Candles"], group=GRP_FGF, tooltip="Until next signal: the level stays in force until the next signal replaces it. Minutes / Candles: it also ends after that many minutes, or that many filter-timeframe candles counted from the signal candle (1 = the signal candle only); then nothing is allowed until the next signal.")
fgfMinutes   = input.int(60, "Minutes", minval=1, group=GRP_FGF)
fgfBars      = input.int(1, "Candles", minval=1, group=GRP_FGF)
fgfCheck     = input.string("Tick", "Check price on", options=["Tick", "Candle open", "Candle close"], group=GRP_FGF, tooltip="When price is compared to the level. Tick: the live price, on every tick (closed candles keep their close). Candle open: each candle's open, decided on its first tick and fixed for the whole candle. Candle close: each candle's close, decided when it closes; while a candle is forming it is judged at its open with the last closed candle's close.")
fgfBandAtr   = input.float(0.25, "No-trade band, ATR mult", minval=0.0, step=0.05, group=GRP_FGF, tooltip="NO TRADE zone around the level: +- this many ATR(14) of the filter timeframe at the signal candle. Inside it price has not chosen a side, so neither buys nor sells are allowed. 0 = no band: above the level BUY ZONE, below it SELL ZONE.")
fgfAgainst   = input.bool(true, "Allow trading against the signal", group=GRP_FGF, tooltip="On: below a BUY signal's level the SELL ZONE allows sells (and above a SELL signal's level the BUY ZONE allows buys). Off: those zones are NO TRADE; only the signal's own direction is allowed, and only once price confirms it.")
fgfAllowBuy  = input.bool(true, "Allow buys", inline="side", group=GRP_FGF)
fgfAllowSell = input.bool(true, "Allow sells", inline="side", group=GRP_FGF, tooltip="Turn one side off completely.")
fgfShowBg    = input.bool(true, "Shade", inline="vis", group=GRP_FGF)
fgfShowLv    = input.bool(true, "Level line", inline="vis", group=GRP_FGF)
fgfSigMark   = input.bool(true, "Signal marks", inline="vis", group=GRP_FGF, tooltip="Shade: green = BUY ZONE (buys allowed), red = SELL ZONE (sells allowed), gray = NO TRADE (inside the band, against the signal when that is off, or that side turned off). Level line: the signal's level, dashed lines: the band edges, names of the zones at the last candle. Signal marks: a triangle where a signal becomes known.")
fgfShowTbl   = input.bool(true, "Status box", inline="tbl", group=GRP_FGF)
fgfTblPos    = input.string("top_right", "", options=["top_right","middle_right","bottom_right","top_left","middle_left","bottom_left","top_center","bottom_center"], inline="tbl", group=GRP_FGF)

GRP_FGS = "Direction score"
fgsShow = input.bool(false, "Show the direction score", group=GRP_FGS, tooltip="In the status box: how often each of three readings of the signals (level side, signal direction, signal reversed) was right on the filter timeframe's candles, 1 and H candles later, buys and sells averaged (50% = a coin flip). Information only: the zones never use it.")
fgsWin  = input.int(500, "Window, filter candles (0 = all history)", minval=0, maxval=500, group=GRP_FGS)
fgsH    = input.int(10, "Longer horizon H, filter candles", minval=2, maxval=100, group=GRP_FGS)

// ---- FlashGold signal inputs (the strategy's, same defaults) ----------------
GRP_FGC = "FlashGold signal: core"
fgfSpreadPts    = input.float(13.0, "Spread pts", minval=0.0, step=0.1, group=GRP_FGC, tooltip="Full spread in points (mintick units). Half of it offsets bid and ask.")
fgfEntryDistPts = input.float(50.0, "Entry distance pts (Points unit)", minval=0.0, step=0.1, group=GRP_FGC)
fgfHoldBars     = input.int(0, "Entry hold bars", minval=0, group=GRP_FGC)
fgfHoldFavPts   = input.float(5.0, "Hold min favorable pts (Points unit)", minval=0.0, step=0.1, group=GRP_FGC)
fgfOnePerBar    = input.bool(true, "One signal per bar", group=GRP_FGC)

GRP_FGB = "FlashGold signal: burst / direction"
fgfDistUnit     = input.string("ATR", "Burst / entry distance / hold unit", options=["ATR", "Points"], group=GRP_FGB, tooltip="ATR: the three thresholds below are multiples of ATR(14) of the filter timeframe. Points: the point inputs in the core group are used.")
fgfBurstAtr     = input.float(0.5, "Burst threshold, ATR mult (ATR unit)", minval=0.0, step=0.05, group=GRP_FGB)
fgfEntryDistAtr = input.float(0.25, "Entry distance, ATR mult (ATR unit)", minval=0.0, step=0.05, group=GRP_FGB)
fgfHoldFavAtr   = input.float(0.1, "Hold min favorable, ATR mult (ATR unit)", minval=0.0, step=0.05, group=GRP_FGB)
fgfBurstPts     = input.float(172.0, "Burst threshold pts (Points unit)", minval=0.0, step=0.1, group=GRP_FGB)
fgfUseBurst     = input.bool(true, "Require burst gate", group=GRP_FGB)
fgfAnyCombo     = input.bool(false, "Allow any combo", group=GRP_FGB, tooltip="If on, TDI parent/zone can approve direction even when burst is weaker.")
fgfDriftBars    = input.int(60, "Prior drift bars", minval=1, group=GRP_FGB)
fgfUseDrift     = input.bool(false, "Use prior drift filter", group=GRP_FGB)

GRP_FGZ = "FlashGold signal: TDI trade zone"
fgfUseZones   = input.bool(true, "Use TDI trade-zone filter", group=GRP_FGZ)
fgfParentTf   = input.timeframe("60", "Parent obedience timeframe", group=GRP_FGZ, tooltip="Calibrated with the parent = the timeframe the signal runs on. Keep it equal to Filter timeframe: a parent above it reads its forming bar live, so it repaints.")
fgfRsiLen     = input.int(14, "TDI RSI length", minval=2, group=GRP_FGZ)
fgfFastLen    = input.int(2, "TDI white fast length", minval=1, group=GRP_FGZ)
fgfMinAligned = input.int(2, "Minimum child zones aligned", minval=0, maxval=6, group=GRP_FGZ)
fgfFlatParent = input.bool(false, "Allow trade if parent is flat", group=GRP_FGZ)
fgfIgnoreNa   = input.bool(true, "Ignore zones without data", group=GRP_FGZ, tooltip="A child zone whose timeframe has no data on this candle is dropped from the active count instead of counting as MIX.")
fgfHtfClosed  = input.bool(true, "Higher-TF zones use the last CLOSED bar", group=GRP_FGZ, tooltip="A child zone on a timeframe HIGHER than the filter timeframe is read from its last closed bar, so history and live agree. Off: such a zone reads its forming bar live, so it repaints.")
fgfUseZ1 = input.bool(true, "Use child zone 1", group=GRP_FGZ)
fgfZTf1  = input.timeframe("60", "Zone 1 timeframe", group=GRP_FGZ)
fgfUseZ2 = input.bool(true, "Use child zone 2", group=GRP_FGZ)
fgfZTf2  = input.timeframe("120", "Zone 2 timeframe", group=GRP_FGZ)
fgfUseZ3 = input.bool(true, "Use child zone 3", group=GRP_FGZ)
fgfZTf3  = input.timeframe("240", "Zone 3 timeframe", group=GRP_FGZ)
fgfUseZ4 = input.bool(false, "Use child zone 4", group=GRP_FGZ)
fgfZTf4  = input.timeframe("480", "Zone 4 timeframe", group=GRP_FGZ)
fgfUseZ5 = input.bool(false, "Use child zone 5", group=GRP_FGZ)
fgfZTf5  = input.timeframe("1", "Zone 5 timeframe", group=GRP_FGZ)
fgfUseZ6 = input.bool(false, "Use child zone 6", group=GRP_FGZ)
fgfZTf6  = input.timeframe("2", "Zone 6 timeframe", group=GRP_FGZ)

// The timeframe the signal runs on ("Chart" = the chart's own).
string fgfTfEff = fgfTf == "" ? timeframe.period : fgfTf
int    fgfTfSec = timeframe.in_seconds(fgfTfEff)

// ===== FLASHGOLD SIGNAL =======================================================
// The strategy's signal logic, unchanged. It runs on the filter timeframe
// (ctxSec = its seconds, used where the strategy compared to the chart).

// TDI direction: fast line (SMA of RSI) rising = 1, falling = -1, flat = 0.
fgfTdiDir() =>
    float r = ta.rsi(close, fgfRsiLen)
    float f = ta.sma(r, fgfFastLen)
    f > f[1] ? 1 : f < f[1] ? -1 : 0

fgfTdiDirPrev() =>
    int d = fgfTdiDir()
    d[1]

// Direction of a child zone. A zone on a timeframe HIGHER than the one the
// signal runs on is read from its last closed bar (fgfHtfClosed).
fgfZoneDir(string tf, int ctxSec) =>
    int dNow  = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tf, fgfTdiDir(), barmerge.gaps_off, barmerge.lookahead_off)
    int dPrev = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tf, fgfTdiDirPrev(), barmerge.gaps_off, barmerge.lookahead_on)
    fgfHtfClosed and timeframe.in_seconds(tf) > ctxSec ? dPrev : dNow

fgfZoneOn(bool use, int dir) =>
    use and (not fgfIgnoreNa or not na(dir))

fgfAlign(int dir, bool on, int side) =>
    on and side != 0 and dir == side ? 1 : 0

// Returns [buy signal, sell signal, signal (entry) price, parent side,
// aligned zones, active zones].
fgfSignal(int ctxSec) =>
    // price model
    float pt         = syminfo.mintick
    float halfSpread = fgfSpreadPts * pt * 0.5
    float bidPx      = close - halfSpread
    float askPx      = close + halfSpread
    float midPrice   = (bidPx + askPx) * 0.5

    // TDI trade zone
    int parentDir = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, fgfParentTf, fgfTdiDir(), barmerge.gaps_off, barmerge.lookahead_off)
    int z1Dir = fgfZoneDir(fgfZTf1, ctxSec)
    int z2Dir = fgfZoneDir(fgfZTf2, ctxSec)
    int z3Dir = fgfZoneDir(fgfZTf3, ctxSec)
    int z4Dir = fgfZoneDir(fgfZTf4, ctxSec)
    int z5Dir = fgfZoneDir(fgfZTf5, ctxSec)
    int z6Dir = fgfZoneDir(fgfZTf6, ctxSec)

    bool on1 = fgfZoneOn(fgfUseZ1, z1Dir)
    bool on2 = fgfZoneOn(fgfUseZ2, z2Dir)
    bool on3 = fgfZoneOn(fgfUseZ3, z3Dir)
    bool on4 = fgfZoneOn(fgfUseZ4, z4Dir)
    bool on5 = fgfZoneOn(fgfUseZ5, z5Dir)
    bool on6 = fgfZoneOn(fgfUseZ6, z6Dir)

    int activeZones  = (on1 ? 1 : 0) + (on2 ? 1 : 0) + (on3 ? 1 : 0) + (on4 ? 1 : 0) + (on5 ? 1 : 0) + (on6 ? 1 : 0)
    int parentSide   = parentDir > 0 ? 1 : parentDir < 0 ? -1 : 0
    int alignedZones = fgfAlign(z1Dir, on1, parentSide) + fgfAlign(z2Dir, on2, parentSide) + fgfAlign(z3Dir, on3, parentSide) + fgfAlign(z4Dir, on4, parentSide) + fgfAlign(z5Dir, on5, parentSide) + fgfAlign(z6Dir, on6, parentSide)

    int  requiredAligned   = math.min(fgfMinAligned, activeZones)
    bool parentFlatAllowed = fgfFlatParent and parentSide == 0
    bool zoneReady         = activeZones == 0 or alignedZones >= requiredAligned

    bool tradeZoneBuyAllowed  = not fgfUseZones or ((parentSide == 1 or parentFlatAllowed) and zoneReady)
    bool tradeZoneSellAllowed = not fgfUseZones or ((parentSide == -1 or parentFlatAllowed) and zoneReady)

    // burst / prior drift
    float atrPts       = ta.atr(14) / pt
    float burstThrPts  = fgfDistUnit == "ATR" ? fgfBurstAtr * atrPts : fgfBurstPts
    float entryDistPts = fgfDistUnit == "ATR" ? fgfEntryDistAtr * atrPts : fgfEntryDistPts
    float holdFavPts   = fgfDistUnit == "ATR" ? fgfHoldFavAtr * atrPts : fgfHoldFavPts

    float burstPts      = (midPrice - midPrice[1]) / pt
    float priorDriftPts = (midPrice - midPrice[fgfDriftBars]) / pt

    bool burstBuy  = burstPts >= burstThrPts
    bool burstSell = burstPts <= -burstThrPts

    bool priorBuyOk  = not fgfUseDrift or priorDriftPts > 0
    bool priorSellOk = not fgfUseDrift or priorDriftPts < 0

    bool rawBuyCandidate  = fgfAnyCombo ? (tradeZoneBuyAllowed and (not fgfUseBurst or burstBuy or parentSide == 1)) : (tradeZoneBuyAllowed and burstBuy)
    bool rawSellCandidate = fgfAnyCombo ? (tradeZoneSellAllowed and (not fgfUseBurst or burstSell or parentSide == -1)) : (tradeZoneSellAllowed and burstSell)

    bool buyCandidate  = rawBuyCandidate and priorBuyOk
    bool sellCandidate = rawSellCandidate and priorSellOk

    // entry hold / virtual stop
    var bool  holdActive    = false
    var bool  holdIsBuy     = false
    var int   holdSignalBar = na
    var float holdSignalMid = na
    var int   lastEntryBar  = na

    float buyEntryPrice  = na
    float sellEntryPrice = na
    bool  buySignal      = false
    bool  sellSignal     = false

    bool canFire = not fgfOnePerBar or na(lastEntryBar) or lastEntryBar != bar_index

    if buyCandidate and canFire
        if fgfHoldBars == 0
            buyEntryPrice := askPx + entryDistPts * pt
            buySignal     := true
            lastEntryBar  := bar_index
        else if not holdActive
            holdActive    := true
            holdIsBuy     := true
            holdSignalBar := bar_index
            holdSignalMid := midPrice
        else if holdIsBuy
            int   elapsedBars    = bar_index - holdSignalBar
            float holdMovePoints = (midPrice - holdSignalMid) / pt
            if elapsedBars >= fgfHoldBars and holdMovePoints >= holdFavPts
                buyEntryPrice := askPx + entryDistPts * pt
                buySignal     := true
                lastEntryBar  := bar_index
                holdActive    := false

    if sellCandidate and canFire
        if fgfHoldBars == 0
            sellEntryPrice := bidPx - entryDistPts * pt
            sellSignal     := true
            lastEntryBar   := bar_index
        else if not holdActive
            holdActive    := true
            holdIsBuy     := false
            holdSignalBar := bar_index
            holdSignalMid := midPrice
        else if not holdIsBuy
            int   elapsedBars    = bar_index - holdSignalBar
            float holdMovePoints = (holdSignalMid - midPrice) / pt
            if elapsedBars >= fgfHoldBars and holdMovePoints >= holdFavPts
                sellEntryPrice := bidPx - entryDistPts * pt
                sellSignal     := true
                lastEntryBar   := bar_index
                holdActive     := false

    if holdActive and ((holdIsBuy and not tradeZoneBuyAllowed) or (not holdIsBuy and not tradeZoneSellAllowed))
        holdActive    := false
        holdSignalBar := na
        holdSignalMid := na

    float signalPx = buySignal ? buyEntryPrice : sellSignal ? sellEntryPrice : na
    [buySignal, sellSignal, signalPx, parentSide, alignedZones, activeZones]
// ===== END FLASHGOLD SIGNAL ===================================================

// Arming, on the filter timeframe: a signal candle sets the level at its
// close. Committed state only (var), so backtests and live agree. aId counts
// the signals.
fgfArm(bool sBuy, bool sSell, float sPx, float sAtr) =>
    var int   aAt  = na
    var int   aBar = na
    var float aPx  = na
    var int   aDir = 0
    var int   aId  = 0
    var float aAtr = na
    if sBuy or sSell
        aAt  := nz(time_close, time)
        aBar := bar_index
        aPx  := fgfLvMode == "Entry price" ? nz(sPx, close) : close
        aDir := sBuy ? 1 : -1
        aId  += 1
        aAtr := sAtr
    [aAt, aBar, aPx, aDir, aId, aAtr]

// Direction score, on the filter timeframe: a rule's direction d at a candle
// is right h candles later when the close has moved that way. Returns the
// balanced share right (mean of the UP and DOWN shares; na until both
// exist) and the number of scored calls, over the window.
fgfHits(int d, int h) =>
    float mv   = close - close[h]
    int   pd   = nz(d[h])
    float upN  = pd == 1 and mv != 0 ? 1.0 : 0.0
    float upH  = pd == 1 and mv > 0 ? 1.0 : 0.0
    float dnN  = pd == -1 and mv != 0 ? 1.0 : 0.0
    float dnH  = pd == -1 and mv < 0 ? 1.0 : 0.0
    int   w    = math.max(fgsWin, 1)
    float wUpN = math.sum(upN, w)
    float wUpH = math.sum(upH, w)
    float wDnN = math.sum(dnN, w)
    float wDnH = math.sum(dnH, w)
    float cUpN = ta.cum(upN)
    float cUpH = ta.cum(upH)
    float cDnN = ta.cum(dnN)
    float cDnH = ta.cum(dnH)
    // (until the window is full: every candle so far)
    float sUpN = fgsWin > 0 and not na(wUpN) ? wUpN : cUpN
    float sUpH = fgsWin > 0 and not na(wUpH) ? wUpH : cUpH
    float sDnN = fgsWin > 0 and not na(wDnN) ? wDnN : cDnN
    float sDnH = fgsWin > 0 and not na(wDnH) ? wDnH : cDnH
    float acc  = sUpN > 0 and sDnN > 0 ? 0.5 * (sUpH / sUpN + sDnH / sDnN) : na
    [acc, sUpN + sDnN]

// The three rules at this filter candle's close, scored 1 and H candles later.
// (Level side: on the signal candle a close exactly AT the level counts as
// the signal's side, as the gate allows it there.)
fgfScore(float aPx, int aDir, int aBar) =>
    int dL = na(aPx) ? 0 : close > aPx ? 1 : close < aPx ? -1 : aBar == bar_index ? nz(aDir) : 0
    int dS = nz(aDir)
    int dR = -nz(aDir)
    [l1, ln] = fgfHits(dL, 1)
    [lh, lhn] = fgfHits(dL, fgsH)
    [s1, sn] = fgfHits(dS, 1)
    [sh, shn] = fgfHits(dS, fgsH)
    [r1, rn] = fgfHits(dR, 1)
    [rh, rhn] = fgfHits(dR, fgsH)
    [l1, lh, s1, sh, r1, rh, ln]

// Each filter candle sends its arm, its conditions, its index, open and close
// time, and the arm, conditions and close time of the candle before it. An
// arm is used only once the candle that made it has closed by this chart's
// clock, so the forming filter candle is never read and nothing repaints.
fgfRead() =>
    [sBuy, sSell, sPx, sPar, sAl, sAc] = fgfSignal(fgfTfSec)
    float fAtr = ta.atr(14)
    [aAt, aBar, aPx, aDir, aId, aAtr] = fgfArm(sBuy, sSell, sPx, fAtr)
    [cL1, cLh, cS1, cSh, cR1, cRh, cN] = fgfScore(aPx, aDir, aBar)
    [aAt, aBar, aPx, aDir, aId, sPar, sAl, sAc, bar_index, time, nz(time_close, time), aAt[1], aBar[1], aPx[1], aDir[1], aId[1], sPar[1], sAl[1], sAc[1], nz(time_close[1], time[1]), cL1, cLh, cS1, cSh, cR1, cRh, cN, cL1[1], cLh[1], cS1[1], cSh[1], cR1[1], cRh[1], cN[1], aAtr, aAtr[1]]

[fpAt, fpBar, fpPx, fpDir, fpId, fpPar, fpAl, fpAc, fpIdx, fpOpen, fpClose, fqAt, fqBar, fqPx, fqDir, fqId, fqPar, fqAl, fqAc, fqClose, fpL1, fpLh, fpS1, fpSh, fpR1, fpRh, fpN, fqL1, fqLh, fqS1, fqSh, fqR1, fqRh, fqN, fpAtr, fqAtr] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, fgfTfEff, fgfRead(), barmerge.gaps_off, barmerge.lookahead_off)

fgfTfText(string tf) =>
    int sec = timeframe.in_seconds(tf)
    sec < 60 ? str.tostring(sec) + "s" : sec < 3600 ? str.tostring(sec / 60, "#.##") + "m" : sec < 86400 ? str.tostring(sec / 3600, "#.##") + "H" : tf
string fgfTfTag = fgfTfText(fgfTfEff)

// Clock: the moment a bar is judged ("Check price on").
//   Tick          a closed bar at its close time; the live bar at the real
//                 clock (every tick), kept inside the bar.
//   Candle open   every bar at its open time (fixed from its first tick).
//   Candle close  a closed bar at its close time; the live bar at its open
//                 time, with the last closed candle's close (see fgfValue).
// Closed bars never repaint in any mode.
bool fgfLiveBar = not barstate.isconfirmed
bool fgfAtOpen  = fgfCheck == "Candle open" or (fgfCheck == "Candle close" and fgfLiveBar)
// The close-time clock (Tick, and closed bars in Candle close). A live bar's
// real clock never reaches the bar's close, nor the close of the filter
// candle still forming (fp on a live bar), so a filter candle is never read
// before its data has closed (delayed data, late ticks).
int  fgfClockC  = fgfLiveBar ? math.max(time, math.min(timenow, nz(time_close, timenow + 1) - 1, nz(fpClose, timenow + 1) - 1)) : nz(time_close, time)
fgfClock = fgfAtOpen ? time : fgfClockC

// The arm in force = the latest filter candle closed by the clock:
//   1  the latest filter candle (fp), once it has closed by the clock
//   2  the candle before it (fq), once that one has closed
//   0  neither (a chart candle longer than the filter candle, judged at its
//      open): the previous chart bar's close-time pick, the latest filter
//      candle closed by this bar's open, as none closes between the two;
//      its index is judged at this bar's open (after a session gap, the
//      next candle)
int fgfSelC = fgfClockC >= fpClose ? 1 : 2
int fgfSel  = fgfAtOpen ? (fpClose <= time ? 1 : fqClose <= time ? 2 : 0) : fgfSelC
// the close-time pick of every bar, kept for the next bar's open (fgfSel 0)
int   fgfCAt  = fgfSelC == 1 ? fpAt  : fqAt
int   fgfCBar = fgfSelC == 1 ? fpBar : fqBar
float fgfCPx  = fgfSelC == 1 ? fpPx  : fqPx
int   fgfCDir = fgfSelC == 1 ? fpDir : fqDir
int   fgfCId  = fgfSelC == 1 ? fpId  : fqId
int   fgfCPar = fgfSelC == 1 ? fpPar : fqPar
int   fgfCAl  = fgfSelC == 1 ? fpAl  : fqAl
int   fgfCAc  = fgfSelC == 1 ? fpAc  : fqAc
// The filter candle the clock falls in (Candles mode): the picked candle when
// it closes exactly at the clock, else the one after it.
int   fgfCIdx = fgfSelC == 1 ? (fgfClockC == fpClose ? fpIdx : fpIdx + 1) : (fgfClockC == fqClose ? fpIdx - 1 : fpIdx)
// the picked candle itself and its close, for the next bar's open (fgfSel 0)
int   fgfCK      = fgfSelC == 1 ? fpIdx : fpIdx - 1
int   fgfCKClose = fgfSelC == 1 ? fpClose : fqClose

int   fgfSigAt  = fgfSel == 1 ? fpAt  : fgfSel == 2 ? fqAt  : fgfCAt[1]
int   fgfSigBar = fgfSel == 1 ? fpBar : fgfSel == 2 ? fqBar : fgfCBar[1]
float fgfLevel  = fgfSel == 1 ? fpPx  : fgfSel == 2 ? fqPx  : fgfCPx[1]
int   fgfSigDir = nz(fgfSel == 1 ? fpDir : fgfSel == 2 ? fqDir : fgfCDir[1])
// the ATR(14) of the signal candle (the no-trade band's unit)
float fgfCAtr   = fgfSelC == 1 ? fpAtr : fqAtr
float fgfSigAtr = fgfSel == 1 ? fpAtr : fgfSel == 2 ? fqAtr : fgfCAtr[1]
int   fgfSigId  = nz(fgfSel == 1 ? fpId  : fgfSel == 2 ? fqId  : fgfCId[1])
// The conditions of the last closed filter candle (status box).
int   fgfPar    = fgfSel == 1 ? fpPar : fgfSel == 2 ? fqPar : fgfCPar[1]
int   fgfAl     = fgfSel == 1 ? fpAl  : fgfSel == 2 ? fqAl  : fgfCAl[1]
int   fgfAc     = fgfSel == 1 ? fpAc  : fgfSel == 2 ? fqAc  : fgfCAc[1]
// The direction score of the last closed filter candle (status box, output).
fgfPickC(float p, float q) =>
    fgfSelC == 1 ? p : q
fgfPick(float p, float q, float cPrev) =>
    fgfSel == 1 ? p : fgfSel == 2 ? q : cPrev
float fgsCL1 = fgfPickC(fpL1, fqL1)
float fgsCLh = fgfPickC(fpLh, fqLh)
float fgsCS1 = fgfPickC(fpS1, fqS1)
float fgsCSh = fgfPickC(fpSh, fqSh)
float fgsCR1 = fgfPickC(fpR1, fqR1)
float fgsCRh = fgfPickC(fpRh, fqRh)
float fgsCN  = fgfPickC(fpN, fqN)
float fgsL1  = fgfPick(fpL1, fqL1, fgsCL1[1])
float fgsLh  = fgfPick(fpLh, fqLh, fgsCLh[1])
float fgsS1  = fgfPick(fpS1, fqS1, fgsCS1[1])
float fgsSh  = fgfPick(fpSh, fqSh, fgsCSh[1])
float fgsR1  = fgfPick(fpR1, fqR1, fgsCR1[1])
float fgsRh  = fgfPick(fpRh, fqRh, fgsCRh[1])
float fgsN   = fgfPick(fpN, fqN, fgsCN[1])
int   fgfIdx    = not fgfAtOpen ? fgfCIdx : fgfSel == 1 ? (time == fpClose ? fpIdx : fpIdx + 1) : fgfSel == 2 ? (time == fqClose ? fpIdx - 1 : fpIdx) : (time == fgfCKClose[1] ? fgfCK[1] : fgfCK[1] + 1)

// The price compared to the level, at that moment.
fgfValue = fgfCheck == "Candle open" ? open : fgfCheck == "Candle close" and fgfLiveBar ? close[1] : close

// Permission window: from the signal candle's close, until the next signal
// (or the minutes / candles run out).
bool fgfArmed  = not na(fgfSigAt) and fgfClock >= fgfSigAt
int  fgfEnd    = fgfLast == "Minutes" and fgfArmed ? fgfSigAt + fgfMinutes * 60000 : na
int  fgfEndBar = fgfLast == "Candles" and fgfArmed ? fgfSigBar + fgfBars : na
bool fgfOpen   = fgfArmed and (fgfLast == "Minutes" ? fgfClock < fgfEnd : fgfLast == "Candles" ? fgfIdx < fgfEndBar : true)

// On the signal candle itself price can sit exactly at the level ("Signal
// close"): there the signal's own side counts as allowed AT the level.
bool fgfOnSigBar = fgfArmed and fgfIdx == fgfSigBar
bool fgfAtBuyLv  = fgfOnSigBar and fgfSigDir > 0 and fgfValue >= fgfLevel
bool fgfAtSellLv = fgfOnSigBar and fgfSigDir < 0 and fgfValue <= fgfLevel

// The zones (see ZONES): above the band BUY ZONE, below it SELL ZONE, inside
// it NO TRADE. With no band the level itself splits them (and on the signal
// candle price exactly at the level counts for the signal's side).
float fgfBand  = fgfBandAtr * nz(fgfSigAtr)
float fgfMt    = syminfo.mintick
float fgfUpLv  = fgfBand > 0 ? math.ceil((fgfLevel + fgfBand) / fgfMt - 1e-9) * fgfMt : fgfLevel
float fgfDnLv  = fgfBand > 0 ? math.floor((fgfLevel - fgfBand) / fgfMt + 1e-9) * fgfMt : fgfLevel
bool  fgfInUp  = fgfBand > 0 ? fgfValue > fgfUpLv + fgfMt / 2 : (fgfValue > fgfLevel or fgfAtBuyLv)
bool  fgfInDn  = fgfBand > 0 ? fgfValue < fgfDnLv - fgfMt / 2 : (fgfValue < fgfLevel or fgfAtSellLv)
// the signal's direction is confirmed while price is in its own zone
bool  fgfSigOk = fgfArmed and (fgfSigDir > 0 ? fgfInUp : fgfSigDir < 0 ? fgfInDn : false)
// a zone allows its side unless it is against the signal and that is off
bool  fgfUpNow = fgfInUp and (fgfAgainst or fgfSigDir > 0)
bool  fgfDnNow = fgfInDn and (fgfAgainst or fgfSigDir < 0)

// Final gates: is a buy / a sell ALLOWED on this bar? (Permission only.)
fgfBuyOk  = not fgfOn or (fgfOpen and fgfAllowBuy  and fgfUpNow)
fgfSellOk = not fgfOn or (fgfOpen and fgfAllowSell and fgfDnNow)

// A new signal became known on this bar; a Minutes / Candles permission ended.
bool fgfNewSig  = fgfSigId > fgfSigId[1]
// What may be done now: 1 BUY ZONE, -1 SELL ZONE, 0 NO TRADE, 2 filter off.
int  fgfZone    = not fgfOn ? 2 : fgfBuyOk ? 1 : fgfSellOk ? -1 : 0
bool fgfEnded   = fgfArmed and not fgfOpen
bool fgfExpired = fgfOn and fgfEnded and not fgfEnded[1] and not barstate.isfirst

// ---- Visuals (optional: delete from here to END if you only want the gates)
fgfPosOf(string s) =>
    switch s
        "top_right"     => position.top_right
        "bottom_right"  => position.bottom_right
        "top_left"      => position.top_left
        "middle_left"   => position.middle_left
        "bottom_left"   => position.bottom_left
        "top_center"    => position.top_center
        "bottom_center" => position.bottom_center
        => position.middle_right

bgcolor(fgfShowBg and fgfOn and fgfOpen ? (fgfBuyOk ? color.new(color.green, 85) : fgfSellOk ? color.new(color.red, 85) : color.new(color.gray, 88)) : na, title="FGF permission", force_overlay=FGF_FORCE_OVERLAY)
plotshape(fgfSigMark and fgfOn and fgfNewSig and fgfSigDir > 0, "FGF buy signal",  shape.triangleup,   location.belowbar, color.lime, size=size.tiny, force_overlay=FGF_FORCE_OVERLAY)
plotshape(fgfSigMark and fgfOn and fgfNewSig and fgfSigDir < 0, "FGF sell signal", shape.triangledown, location.abovebar, color.red,  size=size.tiny, force_overlay=FGF_FORCE_OVERLAY)
plotshape(fgfExpired, "FGF permission ended", shape.xcross, location.top, color.orange, size=size.tiny, text="FGF end", textcolor=color.orange, force_overlay=FGF_FORCE_OVERLAY)

// Level line as a drawing (it does not stretch the price scale). Each signal
// keeps its own line and label, so past levels stay readable. Redrawn every
// bar so a host script's own drawings never garbage-collect the current one.
var line  fgfLn   = na
var label fgfLbl  = na
var int   fgfFrom = na
if fgfNewSig or (na(fgfFrom) and fgfArmed)
    // a new signal: leave the previous signal's drawings where they ended
    fgfLn   := na
    fgfLbl  := na
    fgfFrom := bar_index
if fgfShowLv and fgfOn and fgfOpen and not na(fgfLevel) and not na(fgfFrom)
    int   fgfX1  = math.max(fgfFrom, bar_index - 9000)
    color fgfCol = fgfSigDir > 0 ? color.lime : color.red
    line.delete(fgfLn)
    fgfLn := line.new(fgfX1, fgfLevel, bar_index, fgfLevel, color=fgfCol, width=2, force_overlay=FGF_FORCE_OVERLAY)
    if na(fgfLbl)
        string fgfLastTxt = fgfLast == "Minutes" ? str.tostring(fgfMinutes) + " min" : fgfLast == "Candles" ? str.tostring(fgfBars) + (fgfBars == 1 ? " candle " : " candles ") + fgfTfTag : "until next signal"
        string fgfTxt     = (fgfSigDir > 0 ? "BUY" : "SELL") + " signal " + fgfTfTag + " @ " + str.tostring(fgfLevel, format.mintick) + "\n" + fgfLastTxt
        fgfLbl := label.new(fgfX1, fgfLevel, fgfTxt, style=label.style_label_right, color=color.new(fgfCol, 20), textcolor=color.black, size=size.small, force_overlay=FGF_FORCE_OVERLAY)

// The permission as the status box and the zone names show it: Tick + Minutes
// also ends it by the real clock (the gates, shading and outputs keep the
// candle's clock, see TIMING).
bool fgfDOpen = fgfOpen and not (fgfCheck == "Tick" and fgfLast == "Minutes" and timenow >= fgfEnd)

// The edge of a zone as text: with a band, the band edge (the last NO TRADE
// tick); with no band, the level rounded to the last tick that is not
// allowed, or on the signal candle the first tick that is (">=" / "<=").
fgfEdgeTx(bool up) =>
    bool  incl = fgfBand == 0 and fgfOnSigBar and (up ? fgfSigDir > 0 : fgfSigDir < 0)
    float edge = up ? fgfUpLv : fgfDnLv
    float k    = edge / fgfMt
    float tk   = fgfBand > 0 ? edge : (up != incl ? math.floor(k + 1e-9) : math.ceil(k - 1e-9)) * fgfMt
    (up ? (incl ? ">= " : "> ") : (incl ? "<= " : "< ")) + str.tostring(tk, format.mintick)

// The band's edges (dashed) and the zone names at the last candle.
var line  fgfLnUp = na
var line  fgfLnDn = na
var label fgfZUp  = na
var label fgfZDn  = na
var label fgfZMid = na
if fgfNewSig
    fgfLnUp := na
    fgfLnDn := na
if fgfShowLv and fgfOn and fgfOpen and not na(fgfLevel) and not na(fgfFrom) and fgfBand > 0
    int fgfX2 = math.max(fgfFrom, bar_index - 9000)
    line.delete(fgfLnUp)
    line.delete(fgfLnDn)
    fgfLnUp := line.new(fgfX2, fgfUpLv, bar_index, fgfUpLv, color=color.new(color.lime, 40), style=line.style_dashed, width=1, force_overlay=FGF_FORCE_OVERLAY)
    fgfLnDn := line.new(fgfX2, fgfDnLv, bar_index, fgfDnLv, color=color.new(color.red, 40), style=line.style_dashed, width=1, force_overlay=FGF_FORCE_OVERLAY)
if barstate.islast
    label.delete(fgfZUp)
    label.delete(fgfZDn)
    label.delete(fgfZMid)
    if fgfShowLv and fgfOn and fgfDOpen and not na(fgfLevel)
        bool upAllowed = fgfAllowBuy and (fgfAgainst or fgfSigDir > 0)
        bool dnAllowed = fgfAllowSell and (fgfAgainst or fgfSigDir < 0)
        fgfZUp  := label.new(bar_index + 3, fgfUpLv, (upAllowed ? "BUY ZONE " : "NO TRADE ") + fgfEdgeTx(true), style=label.style_label_lower_left, color=color.new(upAllowed ? color.lime : color.gray, 30), textcolor=color.black, size=size.small, force_overlay=FGF_FORCE_OVERLAY)
        fgfZDn  := label.new(bar_index + 3, fgfDnLv, (dnAllowed ? "SELL ZONE " : "NO TRADE ") + fgfEdgeTx(false), style=label.style_label_upper_left, color=color.new(dnAllowed ? color.red : color.gray, 30), textcolor=color.white, size=size.small, force_overlay=FGF_FORCE_OVERLAY)
        if fgfBand > 0
            fgfZMid := label.new(bar_index + 3, fgfLevel, "NO TRADE (band)", style=label.style_label_left, color=color.new(color.gray, 30), textcolor=color.white, size=size.tiny, force_overlay=FGF_FORCE_OVERLAY)

// Status box (display only; the gates never use it). Judged like the gates,
// at the bar's clock; Tick + Minutes also ends it by the real clock.
var table fgfTable = table.new(fgfPosOf(fgfTblPos), 2, 14, bgcolor=color.new(color.black, 20), border_width=1, force_overlay=FGF_FORCE_OVERLAY)

// the BTC/USD reference scores (out of sample 2025-07 .. 2026-10) of the filter timeframe's bucket
fgsRefTxt(int sec) =>
    int m = math.round(sec / 60.0)
    if m >= 1 and m <= 2
        "1m: level 50/50  signal 50/49  reversed 50/51"
    else if m >= 3 and m <= 10
        "5m: level 51/51  signal 49/49  reversed 51/51"
    else if m >= 11 and m <= 22
        "15m: level 51/51  signal 48/48  reversed 52/52"
    else if m >= 23 and m <= 45
        "30m: level 51/52  signal 49/48  reversed 51/52"
    else if m >= 46 and m <= 90
        "1H: level 50/49  signal 48/50  reversed 52/50"
    else if m >= 91 and m <= 180
        "2H: level 49/52  signal 49/48  reversed 51/52"
    else if m >= 181 and m <= 360
        "4H: level 49/53  signal 49/48  reversed 51/52"
    else if m >= 361 and m <= 720
        "8H: level 51/48  signal 48/51  reversed 52/49"
    else if m >= 1080 and m <= 2880
        "1D: level 49/57  signal 53/43  reversed 47/57"
    else
        "-"

fgsPct(float v) =>
    na(v) ? "-" : str.tostring(v * 100, "#") + "%"
if fgfShowTbl and fgfOn and barstate.islast
    bool   dOpen  = fgfDOpen
    bool   dBuy   = dOpen and fgfAllowBuy  and fgfUpNow
    bool   dSell  = dOpen and fgfAllowSell and fgfDnNow
    string dSide  = fgfSigDir > 0 ? "BUY" : "SELL"
    string dDo    = fgfSigDir > 0 ? "buy" : "sell"
    // what may be done now, and why not when nothing may
    string dWhy   = not fgfArmed ? "waiting for a signal" : not dOpen ? "permission ended" : not (fgfInUp or fgfInDn) ? "price at the level (band)" : fgfInUp and not fgfAgainst and fgfSigDir < 0 ? "above a SELL signal (against it)" : fgfInDn and not fgfAgainst and fgfSigDir > 0 ? "below a BUY signal (against it)" : "that side is switched off"
    string dState = dBuy ? "BUY ZONE - buys allowed, no sells" : dSell ? "SELL ZONE - sells allowed, no buys" : "NO TRADE - " + dWhy
    color  dCol   = dBuy ? color.lime : dSell ? color.red : color.orange
    bool   dConf  = dOpen and fgfSigOk
    bool   dSideOn = fgfSigDir > 0 ? fgfAllowBuy : fgfAllowSell
    string dSigTx = not fgfArmed ? "-" : not dOpen ? "- (permission ended)" : dConf ? (dSideOn ? "CONFIRMED - " + dDo + "s allowed" : "CONFIRMED - but " + dDo + "s are switched off") : "NOT CONFIRMED - do not " + dDo
    int    dSecs  = dOpen and not na(fgfEnd) ? math.max(0, math.floor((fgfEnd - (fgfCheck == "Tick" ? timenow : fgfClock)) / 1000.0)) : 0
    string dLeft  = not dOpen ? "-" : fgfLast == "Minutes" ? str.tostring(math.floor(dSecs / 60), "00") + ":" + str.tostring(dSecs % 60, "00") : fgfLast == "Candles" ? str.tostring(fgfEndBar - fgfIdx) + (fgfEndBar - fgfIdx == 1 ? " candle " : " candles ") + fgfTfTag : "until next signal"
    string dSig   = na(fgfSigAt) ? "-" : dSide + " " + str.format_time(fgfSigAt, "MMM dd HH:mm", syminfo.timezone) + " @ " + (na(fgfLevel) ? "-" : str.tostring(fgfLevel, format.mintick))
    string dPar   = na(fgfPar) ? "-" : fgfPar > 0 ? "BUY" : fgfPar < 0 ? "SELL" : "FLAT"
    string dZones = na(fgfAc) ? "-" : str.tostring(fgfAl) + "/" + str.tostring(fgfAc)
    string dUp    = na(fgfLevel) ? "-" : fgfEdgeTx(true)
    string dDn    = na(fgfLevel) ? "-" : fgfEdgeTx(false)
    table.cell(fgfTable, 0, 0, "FG filter " + fgfTfTag, text_color=color.white)
    table.cell(fgfTable, 1, 0, dState, text_color=dCol)
    table.cell(fgfTable, 0, 1, "Signal (exch tz)", text_color=color.white)
    table.cell(fgfTable, 1, 1, dSig, text_color=fgfSigDir > 0 ? color.lime : fgfSigDir < 0 ? color.red : color.white)
    table.cell(fgfTable, 0, 2, "Signal direction", text_color=color.white)
    table.cell(fgfTable, 1, 2, dSigTx, text_color=not fgfArmed ? color.white : dConf and dSideOn ? (fgfSigDir > 0 ? color.lime : color.red) : color.orange)
    table.cell(fgfTable, 0, 3, "BUY ZONE  " + dUp, text_color=color.white)
    bool   dUpOk  = dOpen and fgfAllowBuy and (fgfAgainst or fgfSigDir > 0)
    bool   dDnOk  = dOpen and fgfAllowSell and (fgfAgainst or fgfSigDir < 0)
    string dOff   = not fgfArmed ? "NO TRADE (no signal yet)" : not dOpen ? "NO TRADE (permission ended)" : "NO TRADE there"
    table.cell(fgfTable, 1, 3, dBuy ? "ALLOWED (now)" : dUpOk ? "allowed there" : dOff, text_color=dBuy ? color.lime : dUpOk ? color.gray : color.orange)
    table.cell(fgfTable, 0, 4, "SELL ZONE " + dDn, text_color=color.white)
    table.cell(fgfTable, 1, 4, dSell ? "ALLOWED (now)" : dDnOk ? "allowed there" : dOff, text_color=dSell ? color.red : dDnOk ? color.gray : color.orange)
    table.cell(fgfTable, 0, 5, "NO TRADE band", text_color=color.white)
    table.cell(fgfTable, 1, 5, na(fgfLevel) ? "-" : fgfBand > 0 ? str.tostring(fgfDnLv, format.mintick) + " - " + str.tostring(fgfUpLv, format.mintick) : fgfBandAtr > 0 and fgfArmed and na(fgfSigAtr) ? "off (no ATR yet at the signal)" : "off", text_color=color.white)
    table.cell(fgfTable, 0, 6, fgfCheck == "Candle open" ? "Candle open" : fgfCheck == "Candle close" ? "Last close" : "Price now", text_color=color.white)
    table.cell(fgfTable, 1, 6, na(fgfValue) ? "-" : str.tostring(fgfValue, format.mintick), text_color=color.white)
    table.cell(fgfTable, 0, 7, "Left", text_color=color.white)
    table.cell(fgfTable, 1, 7, dLeft, text_color=color.white)
    table.cell(fgfTable, 0, 8, "Last " + fgfTfTag + " parent / zones", text_color=color.white)
    table.cell(fgfTable, 1, 8, dPar + " / " + dZones + " aligned", text_color=dPar == "BUY" ? color.lime : dPar == "SELL" ? color.red : color.white)
    if fgsShow
        string hTxt = "next 1 / " + str.tostring(fgsH) + " " + fgfTfTag
        string wTxt = fgsWin > 0 ? "last " + str.tostring(fgsWin) : "all"
        table.cell(fgfTable, 0, 9, "Direction score (" + wTxt + ", " + (na(fgsN) ? "-" : str.tostring(fgsN, "#")) + " level-side calls)", text_color=color.gray)
        table.cell(fgfTable, 1, 9, hTxt + "  (50% = coin flip)", text_color=color.gray)
        table.cell(fgfTable, 0, 10, "Level side (bare level)", text_color=color.aqua)
        table.cell(fgfTable, 1, 10, fgsPct(fgsL1) + " / " + fgsPct(fgsLh), text_color=color.aqua)
        table.cell(fgfTable, 0, 11, "Signal direction", text_color=color.gray)
        table.cell(fgfTable, 1, 11, fgsPct(fgsS1) + " / " + fgsPct(fgsSh), text_color=color.gray)
        table.cell(fgfTable, 0, 12, "Signal reversed", text_color=color.gray)
        table.cell(fgfTable, 1, 12, fgsPct(fgsR1) + " / " + fgsPct(fgsRh), text_color=color.gray)
        table.cell(fgfTable, 0, 13, "BTC 2025-26 (1/10), parent = TF, zones x1/2/4", text_color=color.gray)
        table.cell(fgfTable, 1, 13, fgsRefTxt(fgfTfSec), text_color=color.gray)
// ====================== END FLASHGOLD DIRECTION FILTER =======================

// Exported values (Data Window + linkable as a source from other scripts).
plot(fgfOn and fgfOpen ? 1 : 0, "FGF active", display=display.data_window)
plot(fgfBuyOk ? 1 : 0, "FGF buy allowed", display=display.data_window)
plot(fgfSellOk ? 1 : 0, "FGF sell allowed", display=display.data_window)
plot(fgfLevel, "FGF level", display=display.data_window)
plot(fgfNewSig ? fgfSigDir : 0, "FGF signal (1 buy, -1 sell)", display=display.data_window)
plot(fgfExpired ? 1 : 0, "FGF ended", display=display.data_window)
plot(fgfZone, "FGF zone (1 buy, -1 sell, 0 no trade, 2 off)", display=display.data_window)
plot(fgfOn and fgfOpen and fgfSigOk ? 1 : 0, "FGF signal confirmed", display=display.data_window)
plot(fgsShow ? fgsL1 : na, "FGF score (next candle)", display=display.data_window)

// ═══════════════════ SIGNAL TIMEFRAME (v0.9.2) ═══════════════════
// Everything below up to `shapeMap()` is the detection of v0.9.1, unchanged,
// but wrapped in functions so it can run on the signal timeframe through
// request.security(). The functions must not draw, place orders or read the
// strategy state: they only return numbers. Each signal is returned as the
// TIME of the signal-timeframe candle it last fired on; the chart turns a new
// time into a one-shot event (see newEvt below).
string tfSel    = sigTF == "" ? timeframe.period : sigTF
bool   useSigTF = tfSel != timeframe.period
int    chartSec = timeframe.in_seconds(timeframe.period)
int    tfSec    = timeframe.in_seconds(tfSel)
float  tfRatio  = chartSec > 0 ? tfSec * 1.0 / chartSec : 1.0
// Signal-timeframe bars -> chart bars (for label offsets and the hold check).
off(int n) =>
    math.round(n * tfRatio)

// ───────────────────── WEDGE DETECTOR ─────────────────────
// Pattern at the confirmed bar:
//   offsets 0 .. ctx-1           = context colour  (restored)
//   offsets ctx .. ctx+w-1       = ODD colour      (the wedge)
//   offsets ctx+w .. ctx+w+ctx-1 = context colour  (before)
detect(bool red, bool lime, bool wantRedWedge, int minW, int maxW, int ctx) =>
    int  wHi  = math.max(minW, maxW)
    bool fired = false
    int  wOut  = 0
    for w = minW to wHi
        if not fired
            bool ok = true
            for i = 0 to ctx - 1
                bool v = wantRedWedge ? lime[i] : red[i]
                if not v
                    ok := false
            if ok
                for i = 0 to w - 1
                    bool v = wantRedWedge ? red[ctx + i] : lime[ctx + i]
                    if not v
                        ok := false
            if ok
                for i = 0 to ctx - 1
                    bool v = wantRedWedge ? lime[ctx + w + i] : red[ctx + w + i]
                    if not v
                        ok := false
            if ok
                fired := true
                wOut  := w
    [fired, wOut]

// One state machine per direction. Each call site keeps its own `var` state.
//   0 = idle
//   1 = big candle seen, waiting for the little odd-colour area
//   2 = inside the little odd-colour area
//   3 = flipped back into the zone through a pinch, waiting for the candle in trend direction
// State only moves on closed candles. The "ready" check also runs on ticks so the
// strategy can enter inside the forming candle when "Enter on tick" is on.
contDetect(bool bull, bool red, bool lime, float f, float s, float atr, bool ok) =>
    float body    = math.abs(close - open)
    float gapNow  = math.abs(f - s)
    bool  bigBull = atr > 0 and close > open and body >= contBigAtr * atr
    bool  bigBear = atr > 0 and close < open and body >= contBigAtr * atr
    bool bigBar = bull ? bigBull : bigBear
    bool inZone = bull ? lime : red      // "green zone" (mirror: red zone)
    bool oddClr = bull ? red  : lime     // the little area of the other colour
    bool dirBar = bull ? close > open : close < open
    var int st      = 0
    var int bigAt   = -10000
    var int flipAt  = -10000
    var int oddCnt  = 0
    var int lastSig = -10000
    bool ready = st == 3 and inZone and dirBar and bar_index - flipAt <= contAfter and bar_index - lastSig >= contSep
    bool fired = ready and ok
    if barstate.isconfirmed
        if ready
            // the candle we were waiting for. Checked FIRST so a big green candle can be the signal itself.
            lastSig := bar_index
            st      := 0
        else if bigBar
            // a new big candle restarts the sequence from scratch
            st     := 1
            bigAt  := bar_index
            oddCnt := 0
        else if st > 0 and bar_index - bigAt > contLook
            st := 0
        else if st == 1
            if oddClr
                st     := 2
                oddCnt := 1
            else if inZone and not contNeedRed
                st     := 3
                flipAt := bar_index
        else if st == 2
            if oddClr
                oddCnt += 1
                if oddCnt > contRedMax
                    st := 0            // not "little" any more
            else if inZone
                // the flip bar: the gap on the last red bar or on this bar must be tiny
                if math.min(gapNow[1], gapNow) <= contPinch
                    st     := 3
                    flipAt := bar_index
                else
                    st := 0
        else if st == 3
            if oddClr
                // the lines crossed back: this is turn territory, not CONT. Re-arm as a new little area.
                st     := 2
                oddCnt := 1
            else if bar_index - flipAt > contAfter
                st := 0
    [fired, bar_index - bigAt]

// ── Predict: price where fast and slow cross on the NEXT candle ──
// fast = SMA(rsi, fastLen), slow = SMA(rsi, slowLen). Next candle's RSI that
// makes them equal:  r* = (Ss/slowLen - Sf/fastLen) / (1/fastLen - 1/slowLen)
// with Sf, Ss = sums of the last fastLen-1 / slowLen-1 RSI values. Then invert
// Wilder's RSI to get the close that produces r*.
crossPrice(float upR, float dnR, float sumF, float sumS) =>
    float px = na
    if slowLen > fastLen and not na(upR) and not na(dnR)
        float rStar = (sumS / slowLen - sumF / fastLen) / (1.0 / fastLen - 1.0 / slowLen)
        if rStar > 0.01 and rStar < 99.99
            float a   = rsiLen
            float up1 = upR * (a - 1) / a
            float dn1 = dnR * (a - 1) / a
            float rs  = rStar / (100 - rStar)
            float r0  = up1 + dn1 > 0 ? 100 * up1 / (up1 + dn1) : 50
            if rStar >= r0
                px := close + a * (rs * dn1 - up1)
            else
                px := close - a * (up1 / rs - dn1)
    px

// ───────────── THE WHOLE DETECTION, on one timeframe ─────────────
// Runs on the signal timeframe (request.security). Events are returned as the
// `time` of the candle they fired on; values that the labels need (box top /
// bottom, label y, CONT candle high / low) are captured on that candle.
shapeMap() =>
    // TDI
    float r    = ta.rsi(close, rsiLen)
    float fast = ta.sma(r, fastLen)
    float slow = ta.sma(r, slowLen)
    bool isRed  = invertFill ? fast > slow : fast < slow
    bool isLime = not isRed
    // Signals may fire on any tick (enterTick ON) or only on a closed candle (of this timeframe).
    bool okBar = enterTick or barstate.isconfirmed
    // Areas
    float hiW  = ta.highest(slow, areaLook)
    float loW  = ta.lowest(slow, areaLook)
    float rngW = hiW - loW
    float posW = rngW > 0 ? (slow - loW) / rngW : 0.5
    bool inLow  = posW <= loFrac
    bool inHigh = posW >= hiFrac
    bool botArea = allOn or not botNeedLow  or inLow[botCtx]
    bool topArea = allOn or not topNeedHigh or inHigh[topCtx]
    // Squares
    [botRaw, botWid] = detect(isRed, isLime, true,  botMinW, botMaxW, botCtx)
    [topRaw, topWid] = detect(isRed, isLime, false, topMinW, topMaxW, topCtx)
    var int lastBotBar   = -10000
    var int lastTopBar   = -10000
    var int lastBotWedge = -10000
    var int lastTopWedge = -10000
    bool botOK = botOn and botRaw and okBar and botArea and (bar_index - lastBotBar >= botSep)
    bool topOK = topOn and topRaw and okBar and topArea and (bar_index - lastTopBar >= topSep)
    var int   botT  = na
    var int   botW  = 0
    var float botHH = na
    var float botLL = na
    var int   topT  = na
    var int   topW  = 0
    var float topHH = na
    var float topLL = na
    if botOK
        lastBotBar   := bar_index
        lastBotWedge := bar_index - botCtx
        botT := time
        botW := botWid
        float hh = -1e10
        float ll =  1e10
        for i = 0 to botWid - 1
            hh := math.max(hh, math.max(fast[botCtx + i], slow[botCtx + i]))
            ll := math.min(ll, math.min(fast[botCtx + i], slow[botCtx + i]))
        botHH := hh
        botLL := ll
    if topOK
        lastTopBar   := bar_index
        lastTopWedge := bar_index - topCtx
        topT := time
        topW := topWid
        float hh = -1e10
        float ll =  1e10
        for i = 0 to topWid - 1
            hh := math.max(hh, math.max(fast[topCtx + i], slow[topCtx + i]))
            ll := math.min(ll, math.min(fast[topCtx + i], slow[topCtx + i]))
        topHH := hh
        topLL := ll
    // Turn mark: the wedge warns, the turn confirms (cross back and HOLD).
    var bool botArmed  = false
    var int  botArmBar = 0
    var bool topArmed  = false
    var int  topArmBar = 0
    if botOK
        botArmed  := true
        botArmBar := bar_index
    if topOK
        topArmed  := true
        topArmBar := bar_index
    if botArmed and bar_index - botArmBar > turnMax
        botArmed := false
    if topArmed and bar_index - topArmBar > turnMax
        topArmed := false
    bool holdUp = true
    bool holdDn = true
    for i = 0 to turnHold
        if not (fast[i] > slow[i])
            holdUp := false
        if not (fast[i] < slow[i])
            holdDn := false
    bool crossUpNow  = ta.crossover(fast, slow)
    bool crossDnNow  = ta.crossunder(fast, slow)
    bool crossedUpAt = crossUpNow[turnHold]
    bool crossedDnAt = crossDnNow[turnHold]
    // The cross itself (no hold) — used by the strategy's "At the cross" timing.
    bool botCrossNow = turnOn and okBar and botArmed and crossUpNow
    bool topCrossNow = turnOn and okBar and topArmed and crossDnNow
    // Predict arming, captured BEFORE the turn confirmation clears botArmed/topArmed,
    // so the cross candle itself still counts as armed.
    bool armEvery = armMode == "Every cross"
    bool armL = turnOn and (armEvery or botArmed)
    bool armS = turnOn and (armEvery or topArmed)
    bool botTurn = turnOn and okBar and botArmed and crossedUpAt and holdUp
    bool topTurn = turnOn and okBar and topArmed and crossedDnAt and holdDn
    var int   turnUpT = na
    var float turnUpY = na
    var int   botGap  = 0
    var int   turnDnT = na
    var float turnDnY = na
    var int   topGap  = 0
    if botTurn
        botArmed := false
        turnUpT  := time
        turnUpY  := math.min(fast[turnHold], slow[turnHold]) - 3.0
        botGap   := (bar_index - turnHold) - lastBotWedge
    if topTurn
        topArmed := false
        turnDnT  := time
        turnDnY  := math.max(fast[turnHold], slow[turnHold]) + 3.0
        topGap   := (bar_index - turnHold) - lastTopWedge
    var int botCrossT = na
    var int topCrossT = na
    var int crossUpT  = na
    var int crossDnT  = na
    if botCrossNow
        botCrossT := time
    if topCrossNow
        topCrossT := time
    if crossUpNow
        crossUpT := time
    if crossDnNow
        crossDnT := time
    // Ticks (wick as a compressed cycle)
    float atrV   = ta.atr(atrLen)
    float rngBar = high - low
    float upWick = high - math.max(open, close)
    float dnWick = math.min(open, close) - low
    bool botTick = tickOn and okBar and rngBar > 0 and atrV > 0 and dnWick / rngBar >= botWickRange and dnWick / atrV >= botWickAtr
    bool topTick = tickOn and okBar and rngBar > 0 and atrV > 0 and upWick / rngBar >= topWickRange and upWick / atrV >= topWickAtr
    var int botTickT = na
    var int topTickT = na
    if botTick
        botTickT := time
    if topTick
        topTickT := time
    // CONT
    [contUpRaw, contUpAge] = contDetect(true,  isRed, isLime, fast, slow, atrV, okBar)
    [contDnRaw, contDnAge] = contDetect(false, isRed, isLime, fast, slow, atrV, okBar)
    bool contUp = contOn and contUpRaw
    bool contDn = contOn and contMirror and contDnRaw
    var int   contUpT  = na
    var int   contUpA  = 0
    var float contUpY  = na
    var float contUpHi = na
    var int   contDnT  = na
    var int   contDnA  = 0
    var float contDnY  = na
    var float contDnLo = na
    if contUp
        contUpT  := time
        contUpA  := contUpAge
        contUpY  := math.min(fast, slow) - 3.0
        contUpHi := high
    if contDn
        contDnT  := time
        contDnA  := contDnAge
        contDnY  := math.max(fast, slow) + 3.0
        contDnLo := low
    // Predict: cross price for the next candle of this timeframe.
    float chg  = ta.change(close)
    float upR  = ta.rma(math.max(chg, 0), rsiLen)
    float dnR  = ta.rma(math.max(-chg, 0), rsiLen)
    float sumF = fastLen > 1 ? math.sum(r, math.max(fastLen - 1, 1)) : 0.0
    float sumS = math.sum(r, math.max(slowLen - 1, 1))
    float xPx  = crossPrice(upR, dnR, sumF, sumS)
    [fast, slow, isRed, posW, inLow, inHigh, botT, botW, botHH, botLL, topT, topW, topHH, topLL, turnUpT, turnUpY, botGap, turnDnT, turnDnY, topGap, botCrossT, topCrossT, crossUpT, crossDnT, armL, armS, botTickT, topTickT, contUpT, contUpA, contUpY, contUpHi, contDnT, contDnA, contDnY, contDnLo, xPx]

[fast, slow, isRed, posW, inLow, inHigh, botT, botWid, botHH, botLL, topT, topWid, topHH, topLL, turnUpT, turnUpY, lastBotGap, turnDnT, turnDnY, lastTopGap, botCrossT, topCrossT, crossUpT, crossDnT, armL, armS, botTickT, topTickT, contUpT, contUpAge, contUpY, contUpHi, contDnT, contDnAge, contDnY, contDnLo, xPx] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tfSel, shapeMap())

// A signal time that the chart has not seen yet = the signal fires now, once.
// A higher-timeframe signal repeats its time on every chart candle it covers;
// only the first one fires. Very old times (first candle with data) are ignored.
int staleMs = (2 * math.max(tfSec, chartSec) + chartSec) * 1000
newEvt(int t) =>
    var int seen = na
    bool fresh = not na(t) and (na(seen) or t != seen) and time - t <= staleMs
    seen := t
    fresh

botOK       = newEvt(botT)
topOK       = newEvt(topT)
botTurn     = newEvt(turnUpT)
topTurn     = newEvt(turnDnT)
botCrossNow = newEvt(botCrossT)
topCrossNow = newEvt(topCrossT)
crossUpNow  = newEvt(crossUpT)
crossDnNow  = newEvt(crossDnT)
botTick     = newEvt(botTickT)
topTick     = newEvt(topTickT)
contUp      = newEvt(contUpT)
contDn      = newEvt(contDnT)

// ───────────────────────── PANEL ─────────────────────────
pF = plot(fast, "Fast", color = color.new(color.gray, 30), linewidth = 1)
pS = plot(slow, "Slow", color = color.new(color.silver, 30), linewidth = 1)
fill(pF, pS, color = isRed ? color.new(color.red, 82) : color.new(color.lime, 82))

// ───────────────────────── SQUARES ─────────────────────────
var int nBotSq = 0
var int nTopSq = 0

if botOK
    nBotSq += 1
    int lft = bar_index - off(botCtx + botWid - 1)
    int rgt = bar_index - off(botCtx)
    if showBotBox
        box.new(lft, botHH + 1.5, rgt, botLL - 1.5, border_color = color.new(color.red, 0), border_width = 1, bgcolor = color.new(color.red, 65))
    if showBotLbl
        label.new(rgt, botLL - 2.0, "BOT " + str.tostring(botWid), style = label.style_label_up, color = color.new(color.red, 25), textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)

if topOK
    nTopSq += 1
    int lft = bar_index - off(topCtx + topWid - 1)
    int rgt = bar_index - off(topCtx)
    if showTopBox
        box.new(lft, topHH + 1.5, rgt, topLL - 1.5, border_color = color.new(color.lime, 0), border_width = 1, bgcolor = color.new(color.lime, 65))
    if showTopLbl
        label.new(rgt, topHH + 2.0, "TOP " + str.tostring(topWid), style = label.style_label_down, color = color.new(color.green, 25), textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)

// ───────────────────────── TURN MARK ─────────────────────────
var int nBotTurn = 0
var int nTopTurn = 0

if botTurn
    nBotTurn += 1
    if showTurnUp
        label.new(bar_index - off(turnHold), turnUpY, "▲", style = label.style_label_up, color = color.new(color.yellow, 10), textcolor = color.black, size = size.tiny)

if topTurn
    nTopTurn += 1
    if showTurnDn
        label.new(bar_index - off(turnHold), turnDnY, "▼", style = label.style_label_down, color = color.new(color.orange, 10), textcolor = color.black, size = size.tiny)

// ───────────────────────── TICKS ─────────────────────────
var int nBotTk = 0
var int nTopTk = 0

if botTick
    nBotTk += 1
    if showBotTick
        label.new(bar_index, low, "BOT", style = label.style_label_up, color = color.new(color.yellow, 20), textcolor = color.black, size = size.tiny, force_overlay = true)
if topTick
    nTopTk += 1
    if showTopTick
        label.new(bar_index, high, "TOP", style = label.style_label_down, color = color.new(color.orange, 20), textcolor = color.black, size = size.tiny, force_overlay = true)

// ───────────────────────── CONT ─────────────────────────
var int nContUp     = 0
var int nContDn     = 0
var int lastContUpA = 0
var int lastContDnA = 0

if contUp
    nContUp += 1
    lastContUpA := contUpAge
    if showContMark
        label.new(bar_index, contUpY, "CONT ▲ " + str.tostring(contUpAge) + "b", style = label.style_label_up, color = color.new(color.aqua, 10), textcolor = color.black, size = size.tiny)
    if showContTick
        label.new(bar_index, low, "CONT", style = label.style_label_up, color = color.new(color.aqua, 20), textcolor = color.black, size = size.tiny, force_overlay = true)

if contDn
    nContDn += 1
    lastContDnA := contDnAge
    if showContMark
        label.new(bar_index, contDnY, "CONT ▼ " + str.tostring(contDnAge) + "b", style = label.style_label_down, color = color.new(color.fuchsia, 10), textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
    if showContTick
        label.new(bar_index, high, "CONT", style = label.style_label_down, color = color.new(color.fuchsia, 20), textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny, force_overlay = true)

// ───────── LEGS: continuity vs distance (turn to turn) ─────────
var bool   legOpen = false
var int    legDir  = 0
var float  legP0   = na
var int    legB0   = 0
var float  legPath = 0.0
var string leg1    = "—"
var string leg2    = "—"

if legOpen and barstate.isconfirmed
    legPath += math.abs(close - close[1])

if botTurn or topTurn
    if legOpen
        float dist = math.abs(close - legP0)
        int   bars = bar_index - legB0
        float eff  = legPath > 0 ? dist / legPath : 0.0
        leg2 := leg1
        leg1 := (legDir > 0 ? "UP " : "DN ") + str.tostring(dist, "#.##") + " / " + str.tostring(bars) + "b / eff " + str.tostring(eff, "#.00")
    legOpen := true
    legDir  := botTurn ? 1 : -1
    legP0   := close
    legB0   := bar_index
    legPath := 0.0

// ───────────────────────── STRATEGY ─────────────────────────
// One signal pair only, chosen in S1. Nothing else opens a trade.
bool isTurn      = sigMode == "Turn ▲/▼"
bool isCont      = sigMode == "CONT ▲/▼"
bool turnPredict = isTurn and turnEntry == "Predict (stop at cross price)"
bool turnAtCross = isTurn and turnEntry == "At the cross"
bool contStop    = isCont and contEntry == "Stop past signal candle"
bool longSig  = sigMode == "BOT/TOP square" ? botOK : isTurn ? (turnAtCross ? botCrossNow : botTurn) : isCont ? contUp : botTick
bool shortSig = sigMode == "BOT/TOP square" ? topOK : isTurn ? (turnAtCross ? topCrossNow : topTurn) : isCont ? contDn : topTick
// Predict mode and CONT stop mode place stop orders instead (below); the market-order signals are off.
if turnPredict or contStop
    longSig  := false
    shortSig := false
// Both on one bar = no clear direction, skip.
if longSig and shortSig
    longSig  := false
    shortSig := false

var int nSigL = 0
var int nSigS = 0
if longSig
    nSigL += 1
if shortSig
    nSigS += 1

bool canLong  = tradeDir != "Short only"
bool canShort = tradeDir != "Long only"

// Exit distances in ticks. ATR is taken from the entry candle (or the current
// candle while flat / waiting for a stop order to fill). Chart timeframe.
float exAtr  = ta.atr(exAtrLen)
float tk     = syminfo.mintick
int   eOff   = strategy.position_size != 0 ? math.min(bar_index - strategy.opentrades.entry_bar_index(strategy.opentrades - 1), 499) : 0
float atrE   = exAtr[eOff]
float slTk   = exitUnit == "Points" ? slPts    : slAtrM   * atrE / tk
float tpTk   = exitUnit == "Points" ? tpPts    : tpR      * slTk
float taTk   = exitUnit == "Points" ? trActPts : trActAtr * atrE / tk
float tdTk   = exitUnit == "Points" ? trDisPts : trDisAtr * atrE / tk

calcQty() =>
    float q = qtyFixed
    if qtyMode == "Risk %"
        float slPx = slTk * tk * syminfo.pointvalue
        q := slPx > 0 ? strategy.equity * riskPct / 100 / slPx : 0.0
    q := math.min(q, qtyMax)
    // Margin cap (5% headroom for the fill moving past the close).
    if mgnCap and close > 0
        q := math.min(q, 0.95 * strategy.equity / (close * syminfo.pointvalue * mgnPct / 100))
    math.max(math.floor(q / qtyStep) * qtyStep, 0.0)

float pos = strategy.position_size

// ── Market entries (square, tick, CONT "At signal close", turn "At the cross" / "After hold") ──
if sigBarOK and longSig
    float q = calcQty()
    if pos < 0
        if oppMode == "Reverse" and canLong and q > 0 and fgfBuyOk
            strategy.entry("Long", strategy.long, qty = q, comment = "L " + sigMode)
        else if oppMode != "Ignore"
            strategy.close("Short", comment = "opp signal")
    else if pos == 0 and canLong and q > 0 and fgfBuyOk
        strategy.entry("Long", strategy.long, qty = q, comment = "L " + sigMode)

if sigBarOK and shortSig
    float q = calcQty()
    if pos > 0
        if oppMode == "Reverse" and canShort and q > 0 and fgfSellOk
            strategy.entry("Short", strategy.short, qty = q, comment = "S " + sigMode)
        else if oppMode != "Ignore"
            strategy.close("Long", comment = "opp signal")
    else if pos == 0 and canShort and q > 0 and fgfSellOk
        strategy.entry("Short", strategy.short, qty = q, comment = "S " + sigMode)

// ── CONT "Stop past signal candle": buy stop above the CONT candle / sell stop below it ──
// Placed at the chart close where the CONT signal arrives, above / below the
// SIGNAL timeframe's CONT candle, kept for N chart bars, then cancelled.
var int contStopBar = -10000
var int contStopDir = 0
if contStop and barstate.isconfirmed
    float q = calcQty()
    if pos != 0
        contStopDir := 0          // a stop filled (or another entry is open): nothing pending
    if contUp and canLong and q > 0 and (pos == 0 or (pos < 0 and oppMode == "Reverse")) and fgfBuyOk
        strategy.cancel("Short")
        strategy.entry("Long", strategy.long, qty = q, stop = contUpHi + contStopBuf * tk, comment = "L CONT stop")
        contStopBar := bar_index
        contStopDir := 1
    else if contDn and canShort and q > 0 and (pos == 0 or (pos > 0 and oppMode == "Reverse")) and fgfSellOk
        strategy.cancel("Long")
        strategy.entry("Short", strategy.short, qty = q, stop = contDnLo - contStopBuf * tk, comment = "S CONT stop")
        contStopBar := bar_index
        contStopDir := -1
    else if contStopDir != 0 and bar_index - contStopBar >= contStopBars
        strategy.cancel(contStopDir > 0 ? "Long" : "Short")
        contStopDir := 0
    // Opposite CONT while in a trade and not reversing: close, like the market path.
    if oppMode == "Close only"
        if pos > 0 and contDn
            strategy.close("Long", comment = "opp signal")
        if pos < 0 and contUp
            strategy.close("Short", comment = "opp signal")

// ── Predict: the stop sits at the cross price of the SIGNAL timeframe's next candle ──
// Stop prices with the calibration buffer, rounded to the tick on the safe side.
float stopL = na(xPx) ? na : math.ceil((xPx + predBuf * tk) / tk) * tk
float stopS = na(xPx) ? na : math.floor((xPx - predBuf * tk) / tk) * tk

// Did a trade already open on this candle (filled, maybe even closed again)?
bool enteredThisBar = (strategy.opentrades > 0 and strategy.opentrades.entry_bar_index(strategy.opentrades - 1) == bar_index) or (strategy.closedtrades > 0 and strategy.closedtrades.entry_bar_index(strategy.closedtrades - 1) == bar_index)

if turnPredict and barstate.isconfirmed
    float q = calcQty()
    // Long: armed, fast still below slow -> buy stop at the cross price.
    bool wantL = armL and fast < slow and canLong and q > 0 and not na(stopL) and pos <= 0 and (pos == 0 or oppMode == "Reverse") and fgfBuyOk
    if wantL
        strategy.entry("Long", strategy.long, qty = q, stop = stopL, comment = "L predict")
    else
        strategy.cancel("Long")
    // Short: armed, fast still above slow -> sell stop at the cross price.
    bool wantS = armS and fast > slow and canShort and q > 0 and not na(stopS) and pos >= 0 and (pos == 0 or oppMode == "Reverse") and fgfSellOk
    if wantS
        strategy.entry("Short", strategy.short, qty = q, stop = stopS, comment = "S predict")
    else
        strategy.cancel("Short")
    // Catch-up: the lines crossed at this close but no stop filled -> enter now.
    // Placed after the cancels above so they don't remove it.
    if catchUp and not enteredThisBar
        bool okChaseL = maxChase <= 0 or na(stopL[1]) or close - stopL[1] <= maxChase * tk
        bool okChaseS = maxChase <= 0 or na(stopS[1]) or stopS[1] - close <= maxChase * tk
        if crossUpNow and armL and canLong and q > 0 and okChaseL and (pos == 0 or (pos < 0 and oppMode == "Reverse")) and fgfBuyOk
            strategy.entry("Long", strategy.long, qty = q, comment = "L cross")
        else if crossDnNow and armS and canShort and q > 0 and okChaseS and (pos == 0 or (pos > 0 and oppMode == "Reverse")) and fgfSellOk
            strategy.entry("Short", strategy.short, qty = q, comment = "S cross")
    // "Close only": no reversing stop, close on the actual cross instead.
    if oppMode == "Close only"
        if pos < 0 and armL and crossUpNow
            strategy.close("Short", comment = "opp signal")
        if pos > 0 and armS and crossDnNow
            strategy.close("Long", comment = "opp signal")

// Exits: SL / TP / trailing stop, in ticks from the entry price.
float xSl = slTk > 0 ? slTk : na
float xTp = tpTk > 0 ? tpTk : na
float xTa = trailOn and tdTk > 0 ? taTk : na
float xTd = trailOn and tdTk > 0 ? tdTk : na
strategy.exit("Long X",  from_entry = "Long",  loss = xSl, profit = xTp, trail_points = xTa, trail_offset = xTd, comment_loss = "SL", comment_profit = "TP", comment_trailing = "trail")
strategy.exit("Short X", from_entry = "Short", loss = xSl, profit = xTp, trail_points = xTa, trail_offset = xTd, comment_loss = "SL", comment_profit = "TP", comment_trailing = "trail")

// Turn "Predict" / "At the cross": the cross did not hold -> get out.
// 'Bars the cross must hold' counts signal-timeframe candles; converted to chart candles here.
int turnHoldChart = off(turnHold)
if failExit and (turnPredict or turnAtCross) and barstate.isconfirmed and strategy.position_size != 0
    int held = bar_index - strategy.opentrades.entry_bar_index(strategy.opentrades - 1)
    if held <= turnHoldChart
        if strategy.position_size > 0 and fast <= slow
            strategy.close("Long", comment = "cross failed")
        if strategy.position_size < 0 and fast >= slow
            strategy.close("Short", comment = "cross failed")

// Time stop (chart candles).
if timeStop > 0 and strategy.position_size != 0 and bar_index - strategy.opentrades.entry_bar_index(strategy.opentrades - 1) >= timeStop
    strategy.close_all(comment = "time stop")

// ── Loss reversal (v0.9.1): a trade just closed in the red (or with a tiny profit) -> open the other side ──
// The broker emulator books the exit before the script runs, so on the first
// execution after the exit (the exit candle's close on history, the next tick
// live) strategy.closedtrades has grown by one. Each closed trade is looked at
// exactly once; the last one decides.
var int lossRevSeen  = 0     // closed trades already examined
var int lossRevChain = 0     // reversal trades opened in a row (reset by a winner or a signal trade)
var int nLossRev     = 0     // total reversal trades opened
var int nTinyRev     = 0     // of which after a tiny profit
if strategy.closedtrades > lossRevSeen
    lossRevSeen := strategy.closedtrades
    int    lastIdx   = strategy.closedtrades - 1
    float  lastPnL   = strategy.closedtrades.profit(lastIdx)
    float  lastSize  = strategy.closedtrades.size(lastIdx)
    string lastExit  = strategy.closedtrades.exit_comment(lastIdx)
    string lastEntry = strategy.closedtrades.entry_comment(lastIdx)
    bool   wasRev    = str.contains(lastEntry, "loss-rev") or str.contains(lastEntry, "tiny-rev")
    // Price move of the trade in ticks (independent of qty and commission).
    float  movePts   = math.abs(strategy.closedtrades.exit_price(lastIdx) - strategy.closedtrades.entry_price(lastIdx)) / tk
    bool   tinyWin   = lossRevTiny and lastPnL >= 0 and movePts <= lossRevTinyPts
    bool   wasLoss   = lastPnL < 0 or tinyWin
    // A real winner, or a normal signal trade, starts the chain over.
    if not wasLoss or not wasRev
        lossRevChain := 0
    bool exitCounts = lossRevWhat == "Any losing exit" or lastExit == "SL" or lastExit == "trail"
    string revTag   = tinyWin ? "tiny-rev" : "loss-rev"
    bool chainOK    = lossRevMax <= 0 or lossRevChain < lossRevMax
    // Only when flat and no signal entry was placed on this same run.
    bool flatNow    = strategy.position_size == 0 and not (sigBarOK and (longSig or shortSig))
    if lossRevOn and wasLoss and exitCounts and chainOK and flatNow
        float q = calcQty()
        if lastSize > 0 and canShort and q > 0 and fgfSellOk
            strategy.entry("Short", strategy.short, qty = q, comment = "S " + revTag)
            lossRevChain += 1
            nLossRev     += 1
            nTinyRev     += tinyWin ? 1 : 0
        else if lastSize < 0 and canLong and q > 0 and fgfBuyOk
            strategy.entry("Long", strategy.long, qty = q, comment = "L " + revTag)
            lossRevChain += 1
            nLossRev     += 1
            nTinyRev     += tinyWin ? 1 : 0

// FGF diagnostics (Data Window only, no logic): the entry funnel. Raw = the
// strategy's own signal-entry conditions, ungated, in the active entry mode
// (market, CONT stop, Predict stop, catch-up). The quantity test and the loss
// reversal are not included: both read strategy state consumed inside their blocks.
bool fgdRawLong      = (sigBarOK and longSig and canLong and (pos == 0 or (pos < 0 and oppMode == "Reverse"))) or (contStop and barstate.isconfirmed and contUp and canLong and (pos == 0 or (pos < 0 and oppMode == "Reverse"))) or (turnPredict and barstate.isconfirmed and armL and fast < slow and canLong and not na(stopL) and pos <= 0 and (pos == 0 or oppMode == "Reverse")) or (turnPredict and barstate.isconfirmed and catchUp and not enteredThisBar and crossUpNow and armL and canLong and (pos == 0 or (pos < 0 and oppMode == "Reverse")))
bool fgdRawShort     = (sigBarOK and shortSig and canShort and (pos == 0 or (pos > 0 and oppMode == "Reverse"))) or (contStop and barstate.isconfirmed and contDn and canShort and (pos == 0 or (pos > 0 and oppMode == "Reverse"))) or (turnPredict and barstate.isconfirmed and armS and fast > slow and canShort and not na(stopS) and pos >= 0 and (pos == 0 or oppMode == "Reverse")) or (turnPredict and barstate.isconfirmed and catchUp and not enteredThisBar and crossDnNow and armS and canShort and (pos == 0 or (pos > 0 and oppMode == "Reverse")))
bool fgdBlockedLong  = fgdRawLong  and not fgfBuyOk
bool fgdBlockedShort = fgdRawShort and not fgfSellOk
plot(fgdRawLong      ? 1 : 0, "FGD raw long",      display = display.data_window)
plot(fgdRawShort     ? 1 : 0, "FGD raw short",     display = display.data_window)
plot(fgdBlockedLong  ? 1 : 0, "FGD blocked long",  display = display.data_window)
plot(fgdBlockedShort ? 1 : 0, "FGD blocked short", display = display.data_window)
plot(ta.cum(fgdRawLong      ? 1 : 0), "FGD raw long count",      display = display.data_window)
plot(ta.cum(fgdRawShort     ? 1 : 0), "FGD raw short count",     display = display.data_window)
plot(ta.cum(fgdBlockedLong  ? 1 : 0), "FGD blocked long count",  display = display.data_window)
plot(ta.cum(fgdBlockedShort ? 1 : 0), "FGD blocked short count", display = display.data_window)

// Predicted stop price (blue = buy stop, orange = sell stop) while a stop is armed.
bool showL = turnPredict and armL and fast < slow
bool showS = turnPredict and armS and fast > slow
plot(showL ? stopL : showS ? stopS : na, "Predicted cross price", color = showL ? color.new(color.blue, 0) : color.new(color.orange, 0), style = plot.style_circles, linewidth = 2, force_overlay = true)

// ───────────────────────── TABLE ─────────────────────────
var table t = table.new(position.middle_right, 2, 15, border_width = 1, frame_width = 1, frame_color = color.new(color.gray, 50))

if showTable and barstate.islast
    table.cell(t, 0, 0, "XPW SM v0.9.2 S" + (allOn ? " ALL" : ""), text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.blue, 40), text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(t, 1, 0, isRed ? "RED" : "LIME", text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.blue, 40), text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(t, 0, 1, "Signal TF",   text_size = size.tiny, text_color = useSigTF ? color.yellow : color.gray)
    table.cell(t, 1, 1, (useSigTF ? tfSel : "chart") + " / chart " + timeframe.period, text_size = size.tiny, text_color = useSigTF ? color.yellow : color.gray)
    table.cell(t, 0, 2, "Area pos",    text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(t, 1, 2, str.tostring(posW, "#.00") + (inLow ? " LOW" : inHigh ? " HIGH" : " MID"), text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(t, 0, 3, "BOT squares", text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(t, 1, 3, str.tostring(nBotSq), text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(t, 0, 4, "TOP squares", text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(t, 1, 4, str.tostring(nTopSq), text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(t, 0, 5, "BOT turns",   text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(t, 1, 5, str.tostring(nBotTurn) + "  gap " + str.tostring(lastBotGap) + "b", text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(t, 0, 6, "TOP turns",   text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(t, 1, 6, str.tostring(nTopTurn) + "  gap " + str.tostring(lastTopGap) + "b", text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(t, 0, 7, "BOT ticks",   text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(t, 1, 7, str.tostring(nBotTk), text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(t, 0, 8, "TOP ticks",   text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(t, 1, 8, str.tostring(nTopTk), text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(t, 0, 9, "CONT ▲ / ▼",  text_size = size.tiny, text_color = color.aqua)
    table.cell(t, 1, 9, str.tostring(nContUp) + " / " + (contMirror ? str.tostring(nContDn) : "off") + "  big " + str.tostring(lastContUpA) + "b ago", text_size = size.tiny, text_color = color.aqua)
    table.cell(t, 0, 10, "Leg -1",     text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(t, 1, 10, leg1, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(t, 0, 11, "Leg -2",     text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(t, 1, 11, leg2, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(t, 0, 12, "Trading",    text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(t, 1, 12, sigMode + " / " + tradeDir + (isCont ? " / " + contEntry : ""), text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(t, 0, 13, "Loss-rev",   text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(t, 1, 13, (lossRevOn ? str.tostring(nLossRev) + " opened (" + str.tostring(nTinyRev) + " tiny), chain " + str.tostring(lossRevChain) + "/" + (lossRevMax > 0 ? str.tostring(lossRevMax) : "∞") : "off"), text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(t, 0, 14, "Qty now",    text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(t, 1, 14, str.tostring(calcQty()) + (mgnCap ? " (margin cap)" : ""), text_size = size.tiny)